{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825315-the-town-that-ran-like-clockwork-demon-actual-play","id":825315,"title":"The Town That Ran Like Clockwork - Demon Actual Play","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-07T01:36:40-08:00","id":825315,"title":"The Town That Ran Like Clockwork - Demon Actual Play","content":"Hi everyone. I found doing these write-ups for my last campaign was often as useful for me as much as anything, so I've decided to continue the tradition as my group begins our Demon campaign. This will be the first serious use of second edition rules for most of the group. Most of my campaigns lean heavily towards being sandboxes more than anything, and I don't intend this to be very different, but I wanted to give a shot at tying in a central overarching story as well. So we'll see how that goes. And without further ado...<br /> <br /> The Setting<br /> <br /> The town of Cole's Ford is a small settlement in northern Minnesota. It is isolated, far from any main roads, and even its closest neighbours would be hard pressed to give directions on how to reach it. The people of Cole's Ford have little regular contact with the outside world. The only exception is the logging industry, which dominates the town. A large saw mill operates near the town, and there is a major logging camp only a few hours' drive away. Massive trucks hauling timber regularly make their way through town and out into the world.<br /> <br /> Cole's Ford is more important than it appears. The town teems with Infrastructure. Facilities dominate the skyline, concealed in Twilight, and choirs of angels fill the skies. The town connects with Infrastructure hundreds of miles away, a vital hub in the God-Machine's network. Demons find themselves in the midst of the hornet's nest. Hiding among the humans is hard when they are so few in number, and the God-Machine's heavy presence creates ample opportunities for new Demons to Fall. Covers are precious things indeed, and every Demon walks a knife edge only moments from discovery.<br /> <br /> The Player Characters<br /> <br /> Aegis (Guardian/Saboteur) - Aegis once played the role of the guardian angel. They stepped in front of cars for their ward, diverted the course of falling debris, shielded him from disease, and endured a thousand other injuries and indignities to ensure his safety. But in the midst of all this they fell in love with him and Fell. For a short time they were happy, and Aegis gave birth to a child. But then the hunters came. Aegis's husband was killed, and they went Loud to evade their pursuers and escape with their child. For years Aegis and their daughter, Elise, fled across the United States looking for safety. At every turn they were dogged by Hunter-Killer Angels. At last they arrived in Cole's Ford, and the angel dogging their footsteps Fell rather than complete his mission. Aegis formed the beginnings of the Ring with their former enemy, and has stayed in town out of fear that a sudden departure would see a new angel set after them in pursuit.<br /> Aegis is a survivor more than a fighter, although hardly a pushover in combat. Their current Cover is a lumberjack named Salem, a man of Bolivian descent. In Demon form Aegis is a six-legged clockwork creature of spindly metalwork and rotting flesh, with wings and the ability to launch iron spikes from their limbs. Their powers include Animal Communication, the Hellhound Exploit, Just Bruised, and Like I Built It (the first key in their Cipher).<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://s188.photobucket.com/user/Azahul/media/Aegis.jpg.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i188.photobucket.com/albums/z27/Azahul/Aegis.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> Aegis's player is responsible for each of these pictures.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Axis (Psychopomp/Inquisitor) - Axis has always been inquisitive, so it was only natural that a moment of curiosity was what led to his Fall. He had been ordered to make deliveries to a hospital not far from Cole's Ford. Every delivery disappeared behind a pair of doors, and he burned to know what happened to them. Then one day he followed the delivery, met the angel on the other side, and Fell. Since then he has taken on the Cover of a town librarian, Phil Collins, a carefully groomed man in his late twenties. He manages a privately funded library dedicated to the history of Cole's Ford, while using his position to maintain a collection of books on the occult. He eagerly collects every scrap of information he can on Infrastructure, holding out some hope of one day creating his own to demonstrate his mastery of the God-Machine's own technology.<br /> Through his powers and skills, Axis strives to be competent in many different skills as he can so as to never be without the knowledge he needs, but his focus is on being able to learn new secrets. He has Fungible Knowledge (the first key in his Cipher), Alibi, Eavesdrop, and the Living Shadow Exploit. In his Demon Form he is a being of interlocking gears and dizzyingly complex clockwork, capable of separating into a swarm of mechanical bees if necessary. A grinding maw gapes wide when he is in danger, capable of rendering down any being into their component parts.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://s188.photobucket.com/user/Azahul/media/Axis.jpg.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i188.photobucket.com/albums/z27/Azahul/Axis.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Mr Smith (Messenger/Inquisitor/Integrator) - Mr Smith was once tasked with obfuscating information related to the God-Machine's projects. He was deployed with the cover of an FBI agent, supplied with a human partner, and made his way across the country under the supposed guise of investigating crimes. His true purpose was to spread rumours of alien abductions and UFOs, ensuring that those who had encountered the God-Machine would remain ignorant of what they had seen. But when he came to Cole's Ford, investigating a serial kidnapper who had been operating in the area, he decided that the crime was more important than the mission and Fell. He kept his Cover, Agent John Smith, and threw himself into the investigation wholeheartedly.<br /> Since Falling, Mr Smith has had time to consider his situation. As a Messenger, he has always believed that the world can be changed with the right Input, and found himself naturally drawn towards the Inquisitor Agenda in the belief that the input would be a piece of knowledge. Except that he doesn't believe that knowledge is possible for a Demon to get. As an Angel, Mr Smith thinks he could have had access to the information needed to be safe from the God-Machine forever. When an Angel's mind begins to turn in that direction however, an automatic defence triggers which severs the Angel from the God-Machine server and creates a Demon. By re-Integrating with the Machine with his free will intact, Mr Smith hopes to find that final piece of knowledge he needs to be rid of it forever. He joined the Ring while staking out the local school for signs of the kidnapper, and spotted Elise wielding evidently Demonic powers in an act of spite. He traced her back to Aegis, and the pair struck a deal with Elise's safety in mind.<br /> In his demon form, Mr Smith is a tall, lanky humanoid of dull metal with no discernable facial features. His powers lean towards detecting danger and covering tracks, both for himself and his Ring, and he calls on his Messenger background to insinuate himself among mortals most effectively. Only a handful of people in town are aware of his Cover's position as a member of the FBI, and even among his Ring only Aegis is aware of his mission. His Embeds are Homogenous Memory, Authorised, the Look, and Ellipses.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">No picture of Mr Smith has been done yet.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ms Stitch (Psychopomp/Inquisitor) - Ms Stitch toiled away in a morgue, providing the human materials the God-Machine needed for other projects. She was very good at what she did, and the corpses flowed to meet demand. As the years passed, the orders increased in quantity. They built up, until the day came when she could no longer meet every request. In desperation she turned to murder, culling the living herd to ensure the Machine had its materials, but still the orders kept flowing. In the end it was too much. She Fell, unable to complete her orders.<br /> Much like Axis, Ms Stitch hopes to understand the physics by which the God-Machine operates. Her expertise has always been in flesh, so she seeks to analyse its servants rather than the Infrastructure directly. Angels, Cryptids, Stigmatics, she would put every one of them under the knife if she could. She had worked on the same Infrastructure as Axis, and joined the Ring through him.<br /> In her Demon Form, Ms Stitch resembles nothing so much as an Alien Grey. Holes in her arms can fire deadly bolts when necessary, and a variety of different implants expand her senses beyond the normal range. In her Cover she is Delilah Blake, the owner of the town's small funeral home. Her Embeds are Synthesis (the first key to her Cipher), Ellipses, Sabotage, and the Animate Exploit.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://s188.photobucket.com/user/Azahul/media/Ms%20Stitch.jpg.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i188.photobucket.com/albums/z27/Azahul/Ms%20Stitch.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Veritas (Destroyer/Inquisitor) - Veritas remembers centuries as a Sword wielded by the God-Machine, laying waste to anything his master decreed. He was designed to learn from each encounter, building a repertoire of skills and knowledge to allow him to remove any opposition to the Machine's great plan. His final mission was the execution of a single traitor, a Guardian who had fallen for love. He pursued the Demon across the United States, tracking the being and its daughter to the town of Cole's Ford. He travelled in the form of an army veteran, wandering from town to town, seeking out any scent of his foe. When he reached Cole's Ford, however, the sheer quantity of Infrastructure masked his efforts. His curiosity grew, desiring to learn what each installation was for, and he was lured from his mission. He entered a dark pit humming with Essence, and woke up the next day in hospital as a Demon. The field was empty save for a shattered vessel brimming with Aether, suborned Infrastructure.<br /> Hidden inside the body of Sam, an alcoholic veteran suffering from severe PTSD, he located his one-time prey and struck an alliance. The Ring was born, a collection of individuals he could use to watch his back as he carried out his own investigations to assuage his curiosity. He was programmed to learn, after all, and there is so much he has yet to learn.<br /> In his Demon Form, Veritas is a shifting creature of crystalline structures humming with lightning and fire. Living flesh and nerves bind these crystals to one another, allowing them to adapt and survive against any enemy. His Destroyer nature is intact, fully prepared for combat and the destruction of any enemy. His skills are similarly limited to battle, although since the Fall has begun to study many different disciplines. His Embeds are Shift Consequences, Victory At Any Price (the first key in his Cipher), In My Pockets, and Wave Function Collapse.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://s188.photobucket.com/user/Azahul/media/Veritas.jpg.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i188.photobucket.com/albums/z27/Azahul/Veritas.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Before the first session began, I gave each player knowledge of a single Demon NPC they were familiar with and a handful of rumours they had about possible God-Machine Infrastructure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T02:21:57-08:00","id":825327,"title":"","content":"May I just say that the art of your PCs is fantastic. Aegis in particular is nightmare inducing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T03:39:07-08:00","id":825344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825315-the-town-that-ran-like-clockwork-demon-actual-play?p=825327#post825327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May I just say that the art of your PCs is fantastic. Aegis in particular is nightmare inducing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be sure to pass that on to their player <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I love Aegis to bits myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T18:35:26-08:00","id":825690,"title":"","content":"Creepy!<br /> <br /> I'm not finding Cole's Ford on Google or Google Maps, (this post actually comes up as result #5 on a search for &quot;Town of Cole's Ford&quot;) so I'm guessing Cole's Ford is of fictional origin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T18:47:22-08:00","id":825694,"title":"","content":"That would be correct <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> All my previous games have involved layering the supernatural over a real-world location I was at least passingly familiar with. For this campaign I decided to jump in the deep end and build somewhere from the ground up. It's been a pretty interesting experience. Lots of time spent staring at a blank page thinking &quot;I have no idea how to begin&quot;.<br /> <br /> Fingers crossed that I can actually finish the first session write-up in the next 24 hours. It's been a lot harder to find the time to put it together than I had anticipated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T19:31:56-08:00","id":825714,"title":"","content":"You've got a lot to work with.<br /> <br /> The Great Lakes have all manner of folklore and monsters, so plenty of cryptids and other G-m phenomena, doubly so because you said that Infrastructure exists in high numbers in Cole's Ford.<br /> plus any number of national forest, parks and the Peatland Science and Natural Area. Multiple Reservations are in the area (with Casinos), several military bases just to the south (suspicious lack of publicly listed facilities toward the north of the state, possible evidence of military black sites?) Minneapolis is three and half hours car drive to the south. An <a href=\"http://www.airfields-freeman.com/MN/Airfields_MN.htm\" target=\"_blank\">abandoned airfield</a> in the middle of Superior National Forest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:59:58-08:00","id":826253,"title":"","content":"Session 1<br /> <br /> The sun rose on Cole's Ford on a cold Sunday morning in early January. The sky was clear, but there was thick snow on the ground from the storm the night before. Around town, each member of the Ring went through their usual morning preparations. Church was an important time of the week, the designated time when the Ring could gather in one place to exchange information.<br /> <br /> Mr Smith had established a morning routine after living in the Road Inn North motel for the last few months. He would meet with Farris, the human who ran the motel and one of the few people in town who both knew he was FBI and who he felt he could trust in an emergency, and they would eat breakfast. Farris was a widow, barely keeping the motel afloat thanks to the long term tenancy of Mr Smith and his partner Olivia Sharp. She ate and Mr Smith drank a cup of black coffee in place of food, and Farris passed on a message from the sheriff. His wife was feeling ill, and he wouldn't be at church that day. The sheriff's wife was one of Mr Smith's most values Demon contacts, a Guardian, and he knew that this message meant she feared for her husband's life and was keeping him inside and out of danger just in case.<br /> <br /> Ms Stitch's morning began by checking her home security system for any sign of a break-in. There was a parcel on the front step, wrapped in butcher's paper. She took it inside and opened it, carefully. As always, there was a slip of paper between the fourth and fifth layers. It was orange. According to the prearranged code, that meant it was too dangerous to meet face to face today. The butcher would be lying low. She finished unwrapping the parcel and put the rack of lamb in the fridge.<br /> <br /> Sam woke up before dawn and immediately checked his phone. He had a text from 3:04am from Mr Quiet. &quot;The Loyalists activated at midnight. Objective unknown. I'm going deep, may be out of contact for a while.&quot; Sam deleted the message and then began to blearily rummage through his fridge. He found a bottle of liquor with something still swishing around the bottom. He took a long pull, sprinkled some around his shoulders, and went back to work prying loose the floorboards in his bedroom. He activated In My Pockets to draw out a submachine gun and stored it in the gap for later use, and then went to wait for the pastor's arrival. Taking pity on the poor damaged soldier, Goodenough Jones, the local priest, always made sure to pick Sam up each Sunday so that he would make it to church.<br /> <br /> Getting Elise out of bed in the morning was a trying experience, particularly on Sunday. Eggs and bacon were a necessary bribe to lure her out from under the doona. After that, Aegis had to resort to bribes. This morning proved very expensive. If Elise promised to come to church today, and to come every week for a year, then Aegis would get her a new computer at the first opportunity. Ajax, the bear-sized hellhound Aegis had created to protect their daughter, watched this exchange and whined with a sound like steel tearing until the plates were dropped to the ground for him to lick clean. Before leaving the house, Aegis noticed a text had come through to their second phone. It was from Breeder, a Saboteur of Aegis's acquaintance. Three pictures, each of the same three men in dark suits, their faces blurred. They were taken in different places in the streets of Cole's Ford, with time stamps ranging from one to three am. The words &quot;On Patrol&quot; came to mind, although no text accopanied by the message.<br /> <br /> Axis rolled out of bed a little after seven and got ready for the day to come. He carefully combed his hair in the mirror after a morning shower, and turned on his computer to check the morning news. At seven-thirty, he received a phone call from Will Sacks. Wilma was a waitress at a local restaurant, and the wife of the previous mayor. She was a bit of local celebrity for getting him thrown in prison for assaulting her. She was also a Demon. She sounded worried, mentioning that her own contacts were saying it was going to be a big day, but Axis wasn't comfortable speaking on the phone. His computer screen flickered momentarily, and it was enough to have him cut the call and leave for church as quickly as he could.<br /> <br /> The church service passed quickly. Goodenough Jones, a Nairobian immigrant turned priest, usually kept to a short service during winter. The church had not been designed with winter in mind, with a poor central heating service and large windows to let all the warmth out, and those in attendance were very happy to make for the small community centre next door where they could mingle and chat. Aegis made Elise promise to be careful and keep her eyes open, and sent her off to join the other kids. And then the Ring gathered.<br /> <br /> One by one, they shared the stories they had heard from their contacts. It was clear something was going down, and it seemed that the best lead they had was from Aegis's pictures of the Angel patrol. They decided to meet for lunch at the bar, run by a friend of Salem\u2019s named Joe Moherty.<br /> <br /> The group then split up to mingle with the rest of town, allowing the players to meet and learn about a host of different characters. Axis had heard some strange rumours about Gant Timbre, a maths teacher at the local school, and listened in to the conversation he was having with Hope Hall, the mayor's wife. Unfortunately, Hope was rather dominating the conversation, but Axis did see something that confirmed one of the rumours he had heard. Mr Timbre was always counting, making some small movement to measure the passing of each second. Whether it was a sign he was Stigmatic, a demon, an angel, or something entirely mundane, Axis couldn't be sure. He intruded on the conversation, and Ms Stitch wandered over to distract Hope, Mr Timbre wasn't the easiest person to speak to, but he did let slip that he was planning on visiting the school later that morning.<br /> <br /> Goodenough Jones excused himself from the gathering early. Veritas, on edge and instantly suspicious, decided to shadow him. The priest walked the short distance to his house, the way he held himself suggesting abdominal pain. He went inside. Veritas knocked on the door a few seconds later, but no one answered. The demon backed off from there.<br /> <br /> Aegis spent some time speaking to Joe. Before he took over the bar he'd worked at the saw mill, and a lot of the local workers were regular customers. She extracted a few odd stories from him, but nothing concrete, and nothing about the previous night directly.<br /> <br /> As for Mr Smith, he misinterpreted a signal from Axis earlier and went on guard, largely missing any chance he had to interact with the people there.<br /> <br /> The gathering broke up slowly around mid-morning. Elise asked her father if she could go over to her friend Jess's place. Jess's mother, Hope, was there to take responsibility, and it would keep Elise out of Aegis's hair while they investigated last night's events, so they agreed.<br /> <br /> With a few hours to burn until they were scheduled to meet at the bar, each demon proceeded to carry out some investigations of their own. Ms Stitch had received a warning about the Pie House, a local diner with a Sunday special. The diner was packed, and the smell of cooking wafted from the kitchen. She ordered waffles, observing the people around her. Everything appeared normal. Before leaving she asked for one of the Special Pies to go. One was happily supplied to her, and she took it back to her quarters adjacent to the funeral home. Laying the pie on the slab, she carefully dissected it with forceps and scalpel and dug out a microscope and a variety of chemicals to help her analyse the contents. The hunks of meat were full of strange amino acid chains, describing a symbol too regular to be natural.<br /> <br /> Axis was busy staking out the school. He sat in his car and watched as Gant drove up, got out, and went inside. A few moments later one of the bottom floor lights went on. It stayed on for about five minutes, then turned off. Moments later, a second light turned on. In this manner Gant proceeded through every room in the school, before leaving and driving off. Axis decided to leave it there, and instead drove to meet Will. She would be leaving work now, he figured he could catch her out behind the restaurant and have a private conversation to find out everything he knew.<br /> <br /> Sure enough, Will was right where he expected her to be. To some extent this lowered Axis's already low opinion of her. Predictability and a disregard for security measures were not good qualities in a Demon. They had a brief exchange in French until she agreed to a code phrase to indicate that she was in danger. When questioned further about the morning's phone call, Will told him that her Ring had reported human and angelic agents on the move, although they had been too busy avoiding notice to obtain any identities. Midnight last night must have had something big go down.<br /> <br /> After this, the group began to gather at the bar. Aegis had a brief encounter with Aaron Hart, a hunter preparing to head out to the ridge for a few days while the fine weather held. Being as his brother was her neighbour, Aegis stopped long enough to exchange a few pleasantries and wish him well, before heading inside. There, Ms Stitch shared her discovery with the pies, and Veritas identified her glyph as an ancient symbol indicating an imperative or command. He believed it to be the first component, a symbol to ensure that what followed would be treated as an order.<br /> <br /> Mr Smith then invited Joe Moherty, busy behind the bar, to come and join them for a hand of poker. Using Loose Lips, he was able to draw out confirmation and a few extra details that Joe had picked up from his lumberjack regulars. The road to the logging camps was becoming an object of some distaste for the odd sounds it made at night, and the fact that metal spikes kept showing up to blow tires in passing trucks wasn't helping the mood either.<br /> <br /> That was when they got the phone call. Hope Hall, near hysterical, rang Salem's phone and gasped out that the children were missing. Aegis took a long moment to process this. They hadn't formally introduced their child to the Ring. They got a couple of details from Hope (where? When? How? Although the latter just returned a wailed &quot;I don't know&quot;) and then hung up.<br /> <br /> The Ring were very interested to help their companion. Mr Smith was just about positive that this must have something to do with the kidnapper he had been hunting. Ms Stitch, meanwhile, was privately considering what it would be worth to her studies to have the product of a Demon and a human to test. They made their way to the Hope residence, to find the police had arrived.<br /> <br /> Veritas stayed outside, as Sam wasn't likely to be allowed near a crime scene. The others hurried inside. Ian Moore, the town sheriff, and his wife June were inside. June was comforting Hope, which gave Mr Smith a moment of entertainment. Of course Exigence had worked out an excuse to stay close to her husband, no matter the circumstance.<br /> <br /> The sight of Mr Smith told Sheriff Moore everything he needed to know. Assuming this was part of the kidnapping investigation, Moore ceded his jurisdiction to Smith. They went to the crime scene, Jill Hall's bedroom, and Ms Stitch's Synthesis gave them a detailed rundown of what had happened. Tranquilisers of some kind in their food and drink had knocked the girls out, and they'd been carried from there. Investigating the outside of the building showed evidence that someone had made their way from the kitchen to the bedroom by following the outside wall, and Hope mentioned that she had been leaving the food unattended as she went back and forth between the kitchen and the living room where her husband was suffering one of his migraines.<br /> <br /> Outside, Veritas stumbled up to a deputy on guard duty and tried to find out what was going on. A dramatic failure later and, seeing as he was reeking of alcohol, he was in the back of a patrol car on charges of being a public nuisance.<br /> <br /> Smith decided to canvass the neighbours and find out if they had noticed anything. When the group went outside, Veritas used Shift Consequences on Hope to get himself out of dodge. Hope had been hysterical and eventually the sheriff had no choice but to put her in custody until she calmed down. June went with her, a little reluctantly, but it seemed like she was the only one suited to the babysitting duty.<br /> <br /> Olivia Sharp, Smith's partner, showed up at this point. Between themselves and the sheriff deputies they were able to get a description of a white sedan seen in the area around the time the children had disappeared. It had been seen heading down main street. Mr Smith and Olivia both knew that the usual modus operandi of the kidnapper was to leave town, and fast, so they asked the sheriff to set up a road block and have his other deputies come with them in pursuit. Overhead, storm clouds began to build.<br /> <br /> Aegis wasn't about to be left behind. As the authorities left, she ordered the others into Ms Stitch's van and had her follow. The icy roads made it difficult to keep up, so the rest of the ring was lagging behind. A few miles beyond the town limits, the Agents Smith and Sharp encountered a sheriff's department patrol car maintaining a road block. They pulled over and went to speak to the deputies, Officers Brook and Paylen, who were very insistent that they not go any further. The two deputies were blonde, tall, broad-shouldered men who looked similar enough to be brothers. Smith was almost instantly suspicious, and activated Aura Sight to confirm. Sure enough, the pair registered as angels to his senses. Smith had a brief vision of manifold wings and long cables connecting the two. He passed the compromise check with an exceptional success, and the pair appeared oblivious to his observation. They were even happy to help, as Olivia asked them whether they had seen the white sedan. Taking their covers as deputies seriously, Brook and Paylen gave a detailed description of a car they had turned back not long ago, as well as every detail they could muster on the driver. This included a name, Norman Merriner.<br /> <br /> The sheriff drew a map from his car and, pulling together what they had learned, Smith was able to determine that an old fishing shed up near the lake was the most likely destination. It had started snowing and the wind was beginning to pick up. And then the van containing the other characters arrived. Brook and Paylen closed ranks, but before they could act the sheriff confronted the demons. He ordered them back to town immediately, telling them that this was a job for the authorities. Aegis made a plea that they be allowed to help find their daughter, making a convincing case that it would help in any negotiation. Sheriff Moore seemed torn, but allowed them to come. The others, however, were told to head back to town immediately. Seeing no real alternative, Ms Stitch, Axis, and Veritas headed back to their homes.<br /> <br /> Leaving Brook and Paylen behind, the sheriff seemed to completely ignore them once he made the decision to turn back, the authorities headed down the country road. The deputies were sent to search a few of smaller trails, while Moore and the FBI pushed on to the fishing shed. By the time they reached it the snow was turning into a blizzard and the sheriff ordered his subordinates to head back to town. In the lee of the building they could make out the shadow of a car. Slipping from their vehicles and out into the howling wind, Aegis and Smith crept up on the shed.<br /> <br /> The sheriff took Aegis, who Smith had ordered be armed, around the back of the building in case Norman made a break for it. Smith waited until they had enough time to be in position, and then he and Agent Sharp burst through the front door. The shed was freezing cold, but a small patch of light in the centre showed a thin, terrified man and two shivering girls. Before Norman could react, Smith activated the Look and froze him in place. The sheriff and Aegis came in from behind. Moore and Sharp were yelling at Norman, telling him to drop the knife he was holding, but frozen still Norman could do nothing to react. Then the sheriff slammed into him from behind, breaking Smith's connection. The knife went skittering away into the shadows, and Moore had Norman in handcuffs before anyone else could even reach him. Aegis rushed to Elise, who was pale and dazed with a small trickle of blood running from a blow to her head. Smith checked on Jill Hall, and found her to be cold and scared but otherwise ok.<br /> <br /> There was only one complication. The storm was getting worse. Sheriff Moore, face grim, fought his way back from the car after trying to radio town. They didn't have a choice, he said. They would have to stay the night and wait it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T14:23:33-08:00","id":826272,"title":"","content":"Wonderful, another let's play to consume like the God-Machine consumes Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T14:28:16-08:00","id":826277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825315-the-town-that-ran-like-clockwork-demon-actual-play?p=826272#post826272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wonderful, another let's play to consume like the God-Machine consumes Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Consumes or generates?<br /> <br /> Either way, Subscribed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T02:34:11-08:00","id":826665,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys! If you do have any comments or criticisms, please do tell me. I'm never entirely sure how clear this stuff comes out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825315-the-town-that-ran-like-clockwork-demon-actual-play?p=825714#post825714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've got a lot to work with.<br /> <br /> The Great Lakes have all manner of folklore and monsters, so plenty of cryptids and other G-m phenomena, doubly so because you said that Infrastructure exists in high numbers in Cole's Ford.<br /> plus any number of national forest, parks and the Peatland Science and Natural Area. Multiple Reservations are in the area (with Casinos), several military bases just to the south (suspicious lack of publicly listed facilities toward the north of the state, possible evidence of military black sites?) Minneapolis is three and half hours car drive to the south. An <a href=\"http://www.airfields-freeman.com/MN/Airfields_MN.htm\" target=\"_blank\">abandoned airfield</a> in the middle of Superior National Forest.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was inspiration galore, to be certain. It just took me a lot longer than anticipated to actually find a way to start building the setting.<br /> <br /> Some of that stuff is awesome though. I personally tried to steer clear of the military base thing though. I've been watching too much of the X-Files for that not to feel like a total cliche. <br /> <br /> And in exciting news, we have a picture of Mr Smith! The forum's picture limit won't let me edit it into the original post, so see below:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://s188.photobucket.com/user/Azahul/media/Mr%20Smith.jpg.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i188.photobucket.com/albums/z27/Azahul/Mr%20Smith.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T07:35:01-08:00","id":826804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825315-the-town-that-ran-like-clockwork-demon-actual-play?p=826277#post826277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Consumes or generates?<br /> <br /> Either way, Subscribed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well considering that I am not the one generating the Actual Play, it would be the former lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T21:36:08-08:00","id":828595,"title":"","content":"Session 1.5<br /> <br /> (Aegis and Mr Smith being snowbound was likely to dominate much of our next session, so I decided to sit down with the players instead and wrap up events in the fishing shed before the game tomorrow.)<br /> <br /> Norman hadn't moved since they put him in handcuffs. He sat, still and silent and looking at his lap. The impulse of the humans was to keep him as far from the children as possible, but neither Norman nor the children had heavy winter gear and the only source of heat in the room was the portable stove. Aegis shrugged off their jacket and wrapped the girls in it, while Agent Sharp and Sheriff Moore flanked the children to make sure Norman had no easy way to get to them.<br /> <br /> Sharp muttered to Smith that she wasn't yet sure if they should try to talk to Norman or not. Smith mulled it over. He told Sharp to watch the children, and seated himself next to Norman. He didn't launch straight into trying to get a confession, but instead just tried to get Norman talking. He pulled out a set of playing cards and gently coaxed Norman into drawing a hand. They started to play a game, Smith not even paying attention to what game they were playing, Norman not making eye contact and staring at his feet the entire time.<br /> <br /> Aegis, the only one of the party to have any serious experience as a survivalist, went to work making the shed warmer and alleviating the plummeting temperatures. They used canvas sheets from a damaged sailing skiff to create a rough kind of shelter from the wind, which every so often screamed through cracks in the building's walls and brought a taste of the storm outside with it. With a shelter set up, Aegis built a fire to supplement the warmth from the stove, and sat down next to Elise. She was conscious enough at this point to grip them tightly, but she didn't speak. Everyone watched the game of cards between Smith and Norman, surrounded by the dark and the cold.<br /> <br /> Eventually, Smith's Loose Lips Embed began to draw words from Norman's lips. He spoke about his childhood, of growing up with his mother. She was a recluse, had home schooled him and kept him away from other children his age. He never had a friend, was never good at talking to people. As he got older, it started to become harder to keep his loneliness in check. He would stalk anyone who showed the slightest kindness towards him, growing more and more alienated as his affections were rebuffed time and again. And then his mother died, and he had no one left in his life at all. That was when it grew too much. The kidnapping started, eventually settling on children as Norman identified them as the quickest to trust and befriend. But each and every time the child would demand to be taken home and Norman would need to discipline them. When that did nothing to help build a friendship between them, he would eventually become frustrated at the constant rejection and leave the child somewhere it would be found.<br /> <br /> Aegis listened to this from across the fire, murmuring comforting words to Elise from time to time. She became increasingly responsive, and mentioned that they didn't remember much more than being drugged and then Norman striking her when she woke in his car and screamed. Eventually Elise fell asleep in their arms, while Aegis resolved to exact some kind of punishment upon the human who had dared harm their child.<br /> <br /> Smith had noticed Norman darting occasional looks towards the exits as the conversation wound on. Sharp, Moore, and the two Demons had a quick discussion about sleeping arrangements, namely that someone had to be awake and watching Norman at all times. Smith suggested he be handcuffed to Norman to curtail any escape attempts. Aegis, with no intention of showing their hand too early, volunteered for the second watch. Olivia took the first.<br /> <br /> After an hour, the children, Ian, and Smith were all asleep. Aegis was lying with their eyes open, watching and waiting. The shadows masked Norman's movement though, as he slowly worked Smith's pistol out from its holster. Smith work to the muzzle pressing into his back, and Norman's hissed words.<br /> <br /> &quot;They are whispering again. Can you hear them?&quot;<br /> <br /> Smith smiled into the darkness and, in a low voice dripping with honey, soothed the agitated kidnapper. Without waking the others he talked until Norman realised that the whispers were in his head. Worried but convinced to put his trust in his captor, Norman handed the gun back.<br /> <br /> In order to help Norman, Smith promised to investigate the sounds. The two of them got to their feet. Aegis pretended to be asleep, and Smith gave an easy bullshit excuse to Olivia. The two of them did a circuit of the shed, checking the rafters. One end of the shed went out over the ice in a short jetty, and Smith noticed deep cracks in the ice sheet. At one point they froze, hearing a scratching sound against one wall of the shed, but Smith convinced Norman that it must have been a tree.<br /> <br /> Aegis watched as they settled down again. Another hour or so passed, and it was their turn to go on watch. They waited until Olivia was fast asleep, and picked up their rifle. They went for a walk to stretch her legs, and then lined themselves up to rush Norman. And then they charged.<br /> <br /> Mr Smith had not been sleeping, unconvinced by his own platitudes and worried that there was something in the darkness with them. When Aegis made their move, Smith was up in an eyeblink and crouching over Norman. Aegis swung the rifle to knock Smith out of the way, but Smith kicked out and sent Aegis tumbling to the ground instead. Then he sank his knee into downed Demon's gut, winding Aegis badly. The others started to wake from the scuffle, Norman giving a yelp and hiding behind Smith, and Aegis forced themselves to relax and yield.<br /> <br /> Sheriff Moore walked over and placed a hand on Smith's shoulder. &quot;I hate to say 'I told you so',&quot; he said, looking sternly at Aegis. The three law enforcement officers decided between them that Smith would have to go on watch until midnight, then the Sheriff would take over. Aegis was asked to place themselves as far from Norman as they could get and still stay warm, and to give the Sheriff their gun. And, once again, everyone tried to settle down and sleep. Before they drifted off though, Aegis was able to exact one tiny, petty revenge, as they called out to Norman and described exactly how low his odds were of ever making a friend.<br /> <br /> Smith spent the next few hours staring into the shadows, alone and silent. Norman was awake, but shaking quietly and sobbing in no fit state to speak. Midnight approached. As the second hand of his watch crept towards the apex, the howling wind went quiet. The storm stopped. Everything fell into silence. Smith got to his feet and walked to the window, Norman stumbling silently behind him. He went to look out into the silent night.<br /> <br /> Midnight. Everything went black.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T14:01:49-08:00","id":829865,"title":"","content":"Session 2<br /> <br /> Axis, Veritas, and Ms Stitch retreated to Axis's library to wait out the storm. They took the opportunity to do a little digging. Veritas investigated the strange dark men from the photos Aegis had provided last session, trying to determine if they were Angels recorded in the files. What he found was that the classic &quot;Men in Black&quot; Covers dated back to the 1968 Mothman campaign, and were frequently used by Destroyer Angels with little need to engage directly with humans. It didn't offer any actual information on who the angels wearing the Covers might be.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Axis found that the symbol Ms Stitch had found baked into the meat pie on a molecular level was ancient, drawing on occult symbols used in Mesoamerica more than 2000 years previously. It didn't offer any further clues as to its purpose beyond Veritas's earlier discovery that it was the first part of a command, but the three of them agreed that they would need to see to the Pie House when the others returned.<br /> <br /> One by one, they bedded down for the night in the library. The storm continued to rage outside. Axis was the last to sleep, curled up among a pile of books.<br /> <br /> He woke to find himself in his bed, in his apartment, at home. He stared at the roof. On the outside, everything looked normal. On the inside, Axis was panicking. After he stopped screaming inside, he checked his phone. The date was January 10, Sunday morning. The same as yesterday. He called Ms Stitch. She answered the phone with a, &quot;Happened to you as well, eh?&quot; The two spoke briefly, when they heard a distinct click on the line. Ms Stitch disconnected immediately.<br /> <br /> Across town, Aegis leapt out of bed and rushed to check on Elise. She woke up as they burst into the room, and promptly burst into tears. When she calmed down, it was quite clear that she remembered the previous day. Aegis summoned Ajax to their side and ordered the enormous Hellhound to stay with Elise, and ordered Elise to stay inside. As they were leaving the house to head to Church, they received a text from Breeder. &quot;That explains yesterday.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mr Smith noted that Farris's conversation with him was identical to the previous day, passing on the same message from the sheriff. He figured that Exigence must be worried that acting differently from the previous day might garner attention. He asked Olivia to drop him at the church just as he had the day before.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Veritas discovered that the submachine gun he had secreted beneath his floorboards the day before had disappeared. He waited for the pastor to arrive to drive him to church. When Goodenough Jones arrived, Veritas panicked. He was so focussed on recalling and replicating every word he had spoken the day before that his attempts to speak were stilted and unnatural.<br /> <br /> Axis left his apartment and was heading down the stairs when a voice called out his Cover's last name. &quot;Collins?&quot; The speaker was Jack, a neighbour of his, peering around the corner of his door on the first floor. Axis stopped politely to listen to his neighbour, and Jack asked, without ever leaving his doorway or giving Axis a glimpse of the room beyond it, if he was going to church. When Axis said he was, Jack asked if he could buy some chalk on his way back and leave it outside his door. Axis replied smoothly that of course, he would be happy to run such an errand for a neighbour. Internally, he was running through his memory of yesterday. Yesterday, Jack had come to church. What had changed?<br /> <br /> The group sat through the morning sermon as Goodenough Jones delivered the exact same speech as he had the day before. Aegis tried to use Like I Built It to analyse the church's structure, but instead ended up overloading her own senses with the flood of information. Disorientated, she remained seated as everyone else filed out of the church and went next door to the community centre.<br /> <br /> The rest of the ring met to work out what had happened. It was clear that the previous day was repeating itself. Demons appeared able to recall the previous day's events, most humans seemed unable to do so. Which immediately placed a very large question mark over Axis's neighbour, Jack.<br /> <br /> Veritas remembered that Goodenough Jones was going to leave early, if today played out the same as yesterday. Still suspicious of the priest, he excused himself from the ring and slipped out of the gathering first. He made his way to Goodenough's home on foot.<br /> <br /> As Mr Smith surveyed the room he noted Norman standing among the crowd and watching Jill Hall. Without her friend Elise around, Jill was standing next to her mother as Hope chatted with Gant Timbre. Smith chose to keep his distance for the moment, having no conclusive evidence of the man's intentions. And besides, there was something else that caught his attention. Fletcher Lynch had arrived. Fletcher was the only other guest at the local motel. He had arrived late last week, and had hardly been seen since. Without his daily conversations with Farris, Smith would have been hard pressed to know that Fletcher was in town at all. The man wore a black suit jacket and white shirt. He was pale, with blonde hair and eyebrows, light blue eyes, and no hint of beard. The effect was of someone drained, washed out, colourless. He was making his way through the crowd asking a question to each and every person he spoke to, moving on when they shook his head. Curious, Smith asked the group to move into Fletcher's path.<br /> <br /> &quot;Excuse me, do any of you know a man named Jack Berwick?&quot;<br /> <br /> Most of the ring exchanged blank looks, but Axis had been thinking about Jack all morning. &quot;He's my neighbour.&quot;<br /> <br /> Fletcher appeared suddenly interested, asking where Axis lived. This immediately put the Demon on guard, but he offered to lead the way on his drive home if Fletcher didn't mind waiting while he ran an errand on the way back. Fletcher agreed, and the ring separated. Axis agreed to collect Veritas and meet the others at the Pie House, where they intended to look into the Infrastructure in place there.<br /> <br /> Veritas was having little luck scouting out Goodenough Jones's home, and managed to get himself caught in the act. When the perplexed priest asked what on earth Veritas was doing in his backyard, the Demon promptly launched into a rambling confession of his alcoholism and need for help. Jones ultimately called the sheriff's department to have them take Veritas somewhere safe and secure until he calmed down and sobered up, but when the deputy arrived Veritas used Shift Consequences to have Goodenough Jones escorted away instead. Unfortunately, the Embed failed, and Veritas had to use Victory At Any Price to force a success. The barrage of ensuing Compromise Checks (given that Veritas had already used Victory At Any Price earlier that morning in his first conversation with Jones) left Veritas with a temporary Glitch that prevented him from entering a structure without express permission from the owner.<br /> <br /> Axis picked up some chalk on his way home, and then let Fletcher into the building. They walked up the stairs together, and Axis asked Fletcher why he was looking for Jack. Fletcher answered that he had a letter to deliver. It was vitally important that he give it to Jack in person. They reached Jack's door, and Axis knocked. There was no reply from inside, so Fletcher gave it a try. Still no response. Fletcher apparently resigned himself that he would not be able to deliver the letter personally, so he slipped the note under the door. Axis left the chalk outside and continued upstairs to his apartment, bidding goodbye to Fletcher. Axis paused as he reached the first landing, and listened. A few moments later he heard Jack's voice call out, &quot;I already knew that, arsehole!&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bAxis decided to take a risk. He backtracked until he was standing outside of Jack's apartment and called out, &quot;Jack? You too?&quot;<br /> <br /> There was a pause, and the door opened a crack. Jack peered out. &quot;What are you talking about?&quot;<br /> <br /> Axis tried to feign knowledge of Jack's predicament, but when Jack appeared on the verge of slamming the door he fell back on the one thing he absolutely knew was happening. Time repeating itself. Jack's eyes went wide and he realised Axis was, as he put it, one of the Fallen. Axis's Cover held, and Jack opened the door and ushered him inside.<br /> <br /> Jack's apartment was covered from wall to wall with symbols and chalk lines. There were a dozen concentric rings of warding, Axis recognising them on sight as measures to defend against an Angel or Ghost. Axis stepped carefully as he asked Jack what was going on.<br /> <br /> Jack wasn't concentrating on his guest overly much, still scratching at the floor of his apartment with the chalk. He babbled something about being in service to It, but that It had turned on him. He was defending himself. Axis asked about the letter, and Jack waved him to where the envelop was lying torn open on the floor. Axis picked it up carefully.There were just two things written on it. &quot;11:59:59&quot; and the words &quot;Stay inside&quot;.<br /> <br /> It was at this point that the penny dropped for Axis. Jack was a sacrifice, or a target for assassination. A Destroyer Angel was coming. He checked his watch. It was 11:59 already. There was no way he intended to be here when the Angel arrived. He rushed to the door and threw it open.<br /> <br /> Veritas had made his way to the apartment on foot, but the landlord wasn't present to allow him to enter. He had sent a message to Axis when he was a few blocks away, and was waiting for him to emerge from the building. He was standing there when the hand struck midday.<br /> <br /> Axis stood on the threshold when his aetheric resonance detected an immense energy source suddenly on top of him. A being appeared in front of him, a nightmare vision of glass and steel glimpsed through the maddening fractal reflections of a shattered maze of mirrors. It was there, charging at him, and gone as suddenly as it had appeared. Behind him, he heard a sound like something hard hitting something soft and wet. He turned slowly. What was left of Jack Berwick was splattered against the far wall, a thousand shards of glass embedded in his body. The chalk lines across the apartment looked as if they had been blasted apart. Axis stepped out, shut the door behind him, and left as quickly as he could manage.<br /> <br /> He encountered Veritas outside. In a hurried whisper, Axis conveyed everything he had just seen. The two entertained the idea of using Shift Consequences to redirect the creature's attack into a physical object like the apartment wall instead, but Veritas couldn't enter the building and all of the ways they could think of allowing him to see into Jack's apartment would not be overly discrete for the middle of the day. It would be better to meet the rest of the ring as agreed, and decide how to proceed from there.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Mr Smith was enjoying a lovely chat with the proprietor of the Pie House, Maeve. She was talking about how she used only the freshest of local ingredients in her meat pies, and how she woke up before the crack of dawn every day to prepare them. Ms Stitch had used the distraction to sneak into the kitchen and explore. There wasn't anything overtly supernatural there, until they checked the freezer. Large slabs of red meat lay on metal trays in pools of congealing blood, slowly freezing over. Ms Stitch identified this as the Infrastructure's Aether vent, and quietly connected herself to fill up on the excess energy. Aegis had met with their friend Lala, a fellow lumberjack enjoying an early lunch with his oldest daughter Chloe. Lala was just finishing off a large special pie, to Aegis's dismay. While gently trying to warn Lala off the pies, Aegis was overheard by Maeve and the two got into a flaming row over the edibility of the pies that ended in Aegis being banned from the store. Ms Stitch used the distraction to emerge again from the kitchen, and one by one the ring slipped outside.<br /> <br /> At this point Mr Smith received a phone call from the sheriff alerting him to the fact that Jill Hall had been kidnapped. Smith immediately called Olivia with a description of Norman's vehicle, concocting a story about it having been seen at the scene by the neighbours and matching a vehicle he himself had observed that morning in connection to a suspicious figure. He told Olivia that Norman would be trying to flee town, and urged her to intercept him.<br /> <br /> Veritas and Axis joined the others and shared their story about the attack on Jack Berwick. Smith pointed out that if Jack had been trying to ward his apartment he must have known the Angel being sent to kill him, and more importantly, known and incorporated its Bane into the warding. Of course, the failure of the wards made it entirely possible that he had been wrong, but it still seemed vitally important that they investigate the apartment. From the information provided, Smith worked out that the Angel was operating under a Ban that ensured it could only manifest twice a day for a single second at 11:59:59.<br /> <br /> Even the Broken Clock is right twice a day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T18:39:24-08:00","id":835496,"title":"","content":"Session 3<br /> <br /> Picking right up where we left off, the Ring marched straight to Jack Berwick's apartment and began to poke around. Stitch and Smith picked over the scene. They found a shattered pile of crystal in the midst of the wards, Jack's old service revolver, and, hidden in a locked drawer of his desk, a large pile of documents relating to Jack's service to the God-Machine. They started in the Vietnam War, where Jack had killed an officer in a different division and found that the man wore his own face, and continued into 90s and Jack's decision to settle in Cole's Ford, where he had been responsible for orchestrating the deaths of three separate Demons over the past twenty years. <br /> <br /> Stitch chose to focus on the crystal after Smith alerted her to the fact that it could be the angel's bane. Jack would have needed a bane, or at least something he thought was a bane, in order to even attempt to the warding. Stitch used Synthesis to determine that it had originally been a bizarre crystal sundial, broken at the moment of Jack's death. She reported this fact to the others.<br /> <br /> The investigation was wrapping up, and Veritas and Aegis had already made their way outside, when Smith placed a call to the sheriff's department and alerted Sheriff Moore to the murder. Moore was shocked and sounded overwhelmed. Between the kidnapping, the encroaching storm, and now a bizarre death, it must have felt like the world was turning on him. He said he'd make his way over immediately.<br /> <br /> Axis was furious, not wanting mortal investigators tramping all over his home ground, but Smith responded calmly that to do otherwise would be suspicious. Besides, there was always a chance the day would repeat a third time. If it did, Axis would only have to put up with police for a few hours.<br /> <br /> The group didn't wait for the sheriff to arrive. They locked up the room and made their way to the car. There was still one other lead they needed to investigate. Fletcher Lynch, the man who had given Jack a letter with the time of his imminent death.<br /> <br /> Smith knew that Lynch was staying at the town's motel with him, just a few doors down. The Ring approached the door and Smith knocked. Unfortunately, as the door opened, it became apparent that different members of the Ring had formed their own separate opinions on what was going on and what the plan should be. Aegis and Axis had each come to the conclusion that Fletcher was a God-Machine agent, and when he opened the door Aegis launched itself at him. Fletcher reacted faster than any of the Demons, slamming the door shut again immediately. Axis made his way around the side of the building, while Smith tried to talk Fletcher down. Unfortunately, his sharp and threatening words only made the situation worse. Axis peered through the window on the opposite side of the building, watching Fletcher wedge a chair in position to block the door.<br /> <br /> Smith chose to back away after his failure, and used Homogenous Memory to erase himself from the scene. Veritas and Aegis made an attempt to force the door, but were chased off when Farris DuPour emerged from the office and chased them off. During the commotion, Axis opened the window, manifested a vice-like hand and horrific clockwork jaw, slipped into the room and bowled into Fletcher from behind. In the space of a few moments he had Fletcher pinned to the ground and gagged, warning him in a broken, grinding voice that screaming would mean death. When Farris knocked on the door to ask Fletcher if he was alright, Axis scared Fletcher into sending her off with a vague reassurance that he was ok.<br /> <br /> Alone, Axis tried to get his head around the situation. Fletcher was clearly terrified. More strangely, the impromptu interrogation quickly yielded the fact that he didn't seem to know anything about the God-Machine, Angels, or Demons, let alone the fact that the day was repeating itself or why he hadn't been affected. When asked about the letter, where it came from, Fletcher stammered out that they were from him. He'd had compulsions to write them ever since he was a teenager. He didn't know how he knew when people were about to die, he just knew that sometimes he would lose a few minutes of time and when he came to he'd have a letter, written in his own handwriting, and a burning drive to deliver it.<br /> <br /> Axis gradually relaxed as the conversation wore on. Fletcher didn't come off as a threat, and he was reasonably confident that the man was neither an Angel nor a Demon, or even a cultist of some variety. He reverted to his proper human form as Phil Collins, and took a Compromise Check as he explained the nature of the hidden forces at work in Cole's Ford and his own place in it. Axis felt certain that Fletcher would be of use to him, and persuaded the human to agree to help him. Fletcher couldn't leave town, so his best chance was to work with the Demons to survive his time here. Fletcher was eventually convinced. Since he had no memory of the previous Sunday, Axis asked if there was a way he could quickly gain Fletcher's trust if the day repeated again and Fletcher forgot this conversation. Fletcher offered up the name Carlie Sinclair, the first person he ever had a letter about. He'd kept the letter to himself, she'd died in a car crash a few hours later, and he had never told anyone about it.<br /> <br /> By this point snow had started falling outside, and each of the Demons had plans to return to their respective places of residence. Veritas and Stitch, however, had their own plans for the night based on the expectation that the time loop had not been a one-off occurrence. Veritas intended to stockpile a point of Aether into his phone, to see if it would reset physically if he did so. He placed the Aether in the phone and placed the phone beneath his bed. If it was there when he woke up, then clearly the Aether would have had an effect. Stitch was even more ambitious. Wanting to find out where the meat for the pies at the Pie House was coming from, she intended to find a way to stay awake past the point of midnight. She had a small bolthole secreted in the morgue, and retreated there for the night. Aegis was curled up asleep with Elise long before midnight, but the others were all awake to experience the strange sensation of being rendered instantly unconscious as the clocks struck midnight.<br /> <br /> All, that is, except Stitch. Just as she had hoped, the Bolthole seemed to prevent her body from reverting to its previous state. She emerged in the morgue a few minutes after midnight. The storm that had battered the town had disappeared again. She called the others, waking them one by one, to join her in staking out the Pie House. Axis refused to come, feeling on edge and at risk after his close calls with compromise earlier that day. The others assembled for the stakeout. Veritas discovered, to his delight, that stockpiling his phone had caused it to be unaffected by the day resetting. It lay under his bed where he had left it.<br /> <br /> There was no movement in town as the Demons drove, or in Smith's case walked, through the streets. When they reached the Pie House they split up, with Smith and Stitch going out back and lurking in the shadows around the dumpsters while Aegis and Veritas sat in the comfort of Stitch's van and watched the front. They maintained their vigil for hours until, around four in the morning, there was finally movement. An unmarked white truck rolled up main street and turned into the parking space behind the Pie House. Stitch and Smith disappeared into the shadows as a man wearing a white shirt and blue overalls got out of the truck and started unpacking boxes from the back. Neither of them recognised the man. Maeve came out of the Pie House a few minutes later, once the boxes were stacked on a trolley for her to cart inside. She went to take the cart when the delivery man intercepted her. Stitch leaned in close to listen while Smith sat where he was, not wanting to risk exposure. Stitch heard a sound like hissing static, white noise flowing from the delivery man's mouth instead of words while Maeve stood there as if in trance. After a few minutes the delivery man was done, closed up his truck, and drove away. Maeve wheeled her delivery inside.<br /> <br /> As agreed, Veritas and Aegis began tailing the driver with Aegis at the wheel. They followed him out of town as he took a road that Aegis recognised as leading up to the logging camps, although it did split into dirt and gravel roads leading to different farms and properties around the area. The white truck disappeared around the first bend in the road, and by the time they had caught up their target had disappeared. Aegis put on a bit of speed, looking to catch up. And that was when things got strange.<br /> <br /> The dark twilight of pre-dawn grew darker. The trees on either side blurred together, casting longer and longer shadows until the van's headlights lit only thin tracks across the road ahead. The sound of their engine changed, echoing back at them as if they were driving through a great cavern. And the smell. The cool scent of the forest at night had disappeared. Instead the air was warm, and reeking of motor fumes. Aegis slowed the van, and stopped. They had no idea where they were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T13:50:07-08:00","id":836003,"title":"","content":"Oh, forgot to mention. Mr Smith also revealed, purchased, and activated the second Key in his Cipher this session, unveiling his first Interlock. The Key was Remote Link-Up, and the Interlock (bridging Remote Link-Up and Authorised) was the following:<br /> <br /> Kaleidoscopic Brainwash<br /> Cost: 2 Aether<br /> Dice Pool: Manipulation + Persuasion + Primum vs Resolve + Composure<br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> <i>Light shines forth from Mr Smith\u2019s body, overwhelming the senses of the target mortal with a cavalcade of images and a high-pitched, buzzing sound. This sears an instruction into the target\u2019s mind, compelling them to obey.</i><br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The effect backfires, overwhelming Mr Smith\u2019s senses and inflicting the Insensate Tilt. This also causes a Compromise check (+1 bonus).<br /> Failure: Nothing happens.<br /> Success: The target gains the Fugue Persistent Condition. Mr Smith dictates the circumstances that will trigger the condition. When these circumstances occur, the target automatically fails the Resolve + Composure roll to resist the Fugue state. While in the Fugue state, they will follow a single command no longer than a short sentence to the best of their ability. At the end of the scene, the Fugue Condition is resolved.<br /> Exceptional Success: The Fugue state can trigger a number of times equal to Mr Smith\u2019s Primum before it is resolved.<br /> <br /> As Mr Smith was the only character to start the game at Primum 2, this takes him to Primum 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T03:16:50-08:00","id":842936,"title":"","content":"Session 4<br /> <br /> Aegis triggered Like I Built It to try and determine where they were. Their mind expanded, revealing the true scope of this place they had found themselves in. It was an enormous tunnel, a seemingly natural cavern running the entire width of the continent. The floor of the cavern was paved over, converting the entire expanse into a highway running from east to west beneath the USA. But there was no sign of any entrance or exit, not even any means by which they could have come here.<br /> <br /> The revelation opened Aegis's mind to the next Key in their Cipher, Fire Drill. They turned the key to gain access to their Interlock, Home Is Where The Heart Is, an ability that allowed them to attach occult alarms to the area around them (see the following post for the full write-up).<br /> <br /> There were smaller caves and alcoves branching off from the main cavern every few hundred metres. Aegis and Veritas decided to investigate the closest one. They got back into Aegis's truck and drove. They found two cars parked just outside the alcove, and shut their truck's engine off the moment the other vehicles came into view. The two Demons approached the cars carefully, conscious that they were in unknown territory. There was no one about, but they did find one of the cars unlocked. Rifling through the contents of the car, Veritas found identification belonging to a Colby Hoffman, a young man he vaguely recognised from Cole's Ford.<br /> <br /> The Demons looked towards the entrance of the alcove, a downwards-sloping tunnel that disappeared into the darkness. It seemed unlikely to them that a group of teenagers from the town could have ended up here of their own will. Whatever had happened to them, it was undoubtedly going to be dangerous. Aegis retrieved their rifle from the truck, and they decided to investigate.<br /> <br /> The tunnel descended, making several sharp turns, before ending in a hole covered by an ironwork arrangement resembling a sewer grate. Aegis used their new Interlock to leave a trigger behind them that would sound an alert if someone tried to cut them off and trap them inside. They hauled the sewer grate aside. A dim red light was coming from down below, revealing a ladder. Veritas descended first, noting that the air became more humid as he reached the bottom and lacked the smokey car fumes of the larger tunnel. The Demons reached the bottom and took stock of their surroundings.<br /> <br /> There was a doorway in front of them, covered only with a thin curtain. The red light was coming from behind the curtain. Above the doorway were a number of neon letters of disparate shape, size, and colour, spelling out the words, &quot;The Motel Connection&quot;.<br /> <br /> Veritas took the lead. He seized the curtain and hauled it open. Beyond was a small chamber, filled with blankets and pillows. A group of four young men were tangled together in the midst of it, bare flesh glimpsed in places as they moved together. They did not seem to notice the Demons staring at them. After a moment Veritas grabbed the curtain and shut it again. He and Aegis shared a baffled look.<br /> <br /> They took a few minutes to reevaluate the situation. Veritas opened the curtain again, this time trying to take note of everything besides the sex. The chamber looked like an artificial structure, metal walls in a circular shape at odds with the stone walls of the main tunnel. There was a recess at the back of the chamber, and he realised he could see something moving there. It noticed him too. A voice came from the shadows.<br /> <br /> &quot;Who disturbs the ceremony?&quot;<br /> <br /> The men broke apart with a yelp. Veritas watched as a creature drew itself upright. She was a thing of slick, sweaty flesh and rounded curves. She drew herself upright with impossibly long arms and legs, each tipped with the same three finger-like appendages. She was too tall for the chamber, standing stooped with her naked torso barely concealed by thin wrappings of almost transparent gauze. Her head was bald, lacking nose and nostrils, with a too-wide mouth that opened in a smile as she beckoned Veritas and Aegis to enter the chamber. They could see her many tongues flicking over empty gums, licking her lips as she looked them up and down.<br /> <br /> &quot;Uh, we're lost,&quot; Veritas stammered out. &quot;Do you know the way out?&quot;<br /> <br /> The creature's voice was liquid and suggestive at once. She said that they had found their way to the Understate Route One. Only the Father's servants could come and go as they pleased. The Father's servants, and her own worshippers. The latter was spoken like an invitation.<br /> <br /> The two Demons were feeling more than a little out of their depth. Veritas was emphatically not interested in any worship, and suggested they take their chances on the highway. This seemed to annoy the creature. Her eyes, half-closed throughout this exchange, snapped open and Veritas found himself falling into them. His thoughts were overwhelmed by the sensations that overwhelmed him, leaving him stunned, distracted, as the creature turned her attentions to the more receptive Aegis. Her name was Sister Serenity, Aegis discovered. She drew him in, back to her bed.<br /> <br /> Veritas recovered from his sensory overload and was able to focus enough to study the chamber around him as Aegis kept Serenity and her followers occupied. If the Understate was God-Machine Infrastructure, probably a Facility of some kind, then this chamber did not appear to be a part of it. It was more like Serenity was some kind of parasite, latching on to the Infrastructure to sustain herself.<br /> <br /> The two Demons left the chamber some time later, Aegis feeling rather drained. They explained to Veritas the terms of the agreement they had apparently just entered into. Serenity had some kind of control over the Understate's access codes. Her followers, including Aegis apparently, could come as go as they pleased. She would allow them to leave immediately, and if they ever wished to return they had only to bring her a gift. She prized items representing love and devotion, wedding rings, anniversary presents, and did not particularly care where they came from. Failing that, a small, live animal would do. Or a small, live child.<br /> <br /> Back on the surface, Stitch and Smith had returned to Stitch's home to wait for the others. Around five in the morning, with no sign of the others, they decided to go and wake Axis. They arrived at his apartment block to find Veritas already there, waiting for Axis to answer the intercom and let him inside. He'd dropped Aegis off back at their home and driven out here to speak with Axis about the Understate. He promised to tell the others everything once they were inside.<br /> <br /> They were halfway up the stairs when Stitch thought to check on Jack Berwick. The consensus among the group was that he must still be dead despite the day resetting, why else would the God-Machine go through the effort of killing him? Stitch hurried downstairs and pressed the intercom for Jack's room. There was a long pause, and then a disgruntled voice half-shouted &quot;What?&quot; down the line.<br /> <br /> Stitch, assuming that Jack would remember the day before, made a passing reference to him being alive again. This seemed to confuse Jack, and he quickly stopped replying to Stitch's messages. Axis decided to try and remedy the situation. He knocked on the order, asking Jack to let him in. The door opened a crack, and Axis quickly spun some story about a stranger in the lobby spinning stories about Jack's impending death. Jack let Axis inside, and a quick conversation made Axis reasonably sure that Jack didn't remember the previous day. In fact, Jack seemed not to know his life was in danger at all. Axis saw that Jack had his service revolver on him however, and it was quite clear that the man intended to head downstairs and sort out the threat on his own. Axis was able to talk him down, pretended to call the police, and continued to try and get Jack to reveal what he knew was going on. Jack largely stonewalled him though, so eventually Axis went upstairs and placed an actual call to the police to maintain his cover.<br /> <br /> After that, the group spoke about the Understate at some length. Smith advocated against attempts to destroy it, arguing that if it could be made to work for them then it could be a useful asset indeed. The others were less inclined to leave such a significant piece of Infrastructure standing, although Axis did like Smith's idea that it could be an escape route out of town if things went south. Eventually the group disbanded without a conclusive stance being reached and agreed to reconvene at the community centre after church with Aegis.<br /> <br /> Aegis took Elise and Ajax on a brief hunting trip to scrounge up a rabbit, in case they needed an offering for Sister Serenity. Elise promised to check the snares throughout the day, and Aegis joined the others at the church. Together they sat through the same sermon they had been listening to for the last few days. After church they watched Goodenough Jones excuse himself early, Hope gossip at Mr Timbre, and the rest of the routine they were becoming quickly familiar with. Axis left early and called Fletcher.<br /> <br /> &quot;Carlie Sinclair.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Excuse me?&quot; The abrupt start to the conversation clearly threw Fletcher, kept him off-balance. Axis explained that he knew that Fletcher might not remember him, but that Fletcher himself had given him the name to persuade Fletcher to trust him. He asked Fletcher if he had a letter.<br /> <br /> &quot;Wait, are you Chuck Davis?&quot; Axis frowned. The name was only barely familiar. He found out that Fletcher had written a letter to a man named Chuck Davis this day, instead of Jack Berwick. The letter read &quot;11:59:59, stay out of the woods&quot;. Axis thanks Fletcher profusely and hung up, hurrying inside to relay the information to the ring.<br /> <br /> Aegis recognised the name. Chuck Davis was a truck driver responsible for hauling logs from the logging camp to the town saw mill. They went around the community centre asking if there was anyone who might know where Chuck might be found. Joe Moherty ended up giving Aegis their best lead, telling them that if Chuck wasn't at home drinking then he might be out near the woods. Last night (the Saturday before the Sundays started repeating, presumably) Chuck had apparently been in Joe's bar swearing that if he caught whoever was putting spikes on the road, he would kill them.<br /> <br /> The ring promptly drove out to the woods. They found a ute with empty beer bottles on the passenger seat parked close to the start of the road that led up to the camp. Veritas and Axis stood watch over the vehicle, the other three proceeded on foot to see if they could track Chuck, with Aegis taking the lead. It was already past 10.<br /> <br /> They never found him alive. It was well past midday by the time Stitch, Smith, and Aegis came upon a bloodied, beaten young woman curled into a ball next to Chuck's body. Chuck had a gunshot wound starting beneath his jaw that had handily removed the top of his head. Smith gently drew the woman aside to talk to her, while Stitch used Synthesis on the scene. They soon pieced together what had happened. The woman was named Desley Grant. She was eighteen, an ardent environmentalist. She'd taken to placing caltrops on the road to disrupt the logging industry. Chuck had found her and her bag full of twisted metal, Aegis found the bag in question not far away, and started to beat her with the butt of his rifle. She'd been terrified that he was going to kill her. Then everything slowed down. She grabbed at Chuck's gun and wrestled for it, feeling strength well up from hitherto unknown reserves. During the struggle the weapon went off. The next thing she knew she was standing over Chuck, his blood on her hands.<br /> <br /> They made their way back to the others with Desley in tow. Smith found messages on his phone from the Sheriff, one about the death of Jack Berwick (he'd been found dead in his apartment in circumstances similar to what had happened to him the previous day) and one regarding a kidnapping. With an internal groan Smith placed a phone call to the Sheriff and explained all the information he had on Norman. He also reported the death in the forest, and told him that he would bring Desley to the station in person. The ring made another plan to track the delivery van for the Pie House the next morning and, since they had mostly been running without sleep for more than a day, decided to head back to their respective homes to sleep.<br /> <br /> Smith and Axis were the exceptions. Smith made a phone call to an Integrator of his acquaintance named Exigence. She would be able to broker a deal with the God-Machine for him in return for information he had to hand. Smith revealed that he knew of a mortal, Fletcher Lynch, who had known of Jack Berwick's original death in advance. What he wanted in exchange for this information was the removal of security on the Pie House. Exigence indicated that she could make this deal.<br /> <br /> Across town, Axis was hard at work studying. He found passing reference in some of his older texts regarding a story of a medieval village where a host of people died at the stroke of midday. Supposedly, this came after, or possibly before, the town disappeared for many years. When it was found again those who lived there appeared not to have aged or noticed the passing of time, and that the day of the great tragedy had been only days before.<br /> <br /> Axis almost fell from his chair when he read this. It seemed that he had stumbled upon the God-Machine's plan, the reason for time repeating itself. He was convinced that another person would die with every passing day. Having heard about Jack's death from Smith, it seemed apparent to him that the deaths from preceding days would reoccur on top of each new death. When the fatalities approached critical mass, the town would be frozen in time for years, possibly even longer. Why the God-Machine was attempting this was still unclear, but the stakes were becoming obvious to him.<br /> <br /> That night, Aegis, Elise, Ajax, and a rabbit caught in their snares all bunked down in Aegis's hidden bolthole in the woods. When midnight struck, Aegis emerged from the bolthole with the rabbit and called the other members of the ring to wake them. Smith was the first to arrive at the Pie House, slipping through the unlocked front door and accessing the freezer to drain it dry of Aether and fill his personal stores. He was waiting outside when the others arrived, and they settled down in Stitch's van to wait for the arrival of the Deliverer.<br /> <br /> Sure enough, at 4pm, the plain white delivery van made its delivery. Veritas shadowed it around the corner and activated Tag and Release on the van, before coming back to join the others. They then tailed it out of town, and as before they followed it into the Understate without any need for the rabbit. Now that they were expecting the transition they were able to stay on the van's tail as it drove along Route 1. They were driving in the dark, following the lights ahead, for about half an hour before they saw a new pair of lights approaching. Blue and red, flashing on and off. The delivery van started to slow, forcing them to slow with it. Finally it came to a stop, just as a sheriff's department patrol car pulled up next to it. The doors opened, and the wings emerged.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://s188.photobucket.com/user/Azahul/media/The%20Highway%20Patrol_1.jpg.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i188.photobucket.com/albums/z27/Azahul/The%20Highway%20Patrol_1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> Again, courtesy of Aegis's player.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The two creatures were like biblical Seraphim, clusters of wings around a central point, but instead of a human head the wings were arranged around a clockwork mass of gears and piping forming a great cavernous maw. The two beings seemed to unfold as they left the car, their wingspan too large to fit inside the vehicle they had just exited. They converged on the delivery van, and Axis attempted to use Eavesdrop to determine what was being said. &quot;Present clearance&quot;, appeared to be the gist of it. The conversation was brief, and the delivery van continued on its way.<br /> <br /> At that point the angels turned towards the Demon's own van. They approached slowly, flanking the vehicle. Smith swapped seats with Veritas so that he was in the passenger seat, and wound down the window. A voice spoke with the hiss of steam and rattle of clanking pipes, although it was hard to tell which of the two beings were the source of the voice.<br /> <br /> &quot;Present clearance authorising your unit's use of Understate Route 1.&quot;<br /> <br /> Smith smiled easily, activating the Authorised Embed as he stared down the angel. &quot;We're security detail.&quot; He indicated the receding delivery van.<br /> <br /> This seemed to throw the angels. They paused. &quot;There has been no communication regarding the assigning of security resources to this project.&quot; A pause. &quot;You may proceed.&quot;<br /> <br /> The angels moved away. The demons took a moment to process the sudden retreat. Then Stitch started up the engine and they hurried to catch up to the delivery van. The patrol car receded behind them.<br /> <br /> Some time later, they watched the delivery van pull over into a car park lit by gas lamps. Rows of identical white vans sat in the car park. The Deliverer did not emerge from its van. They pulled over to watch. It didn't look like this was where the meat was coming from, but the van would need to go there some time. The only question now was how long they would need to wait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 03-06-2016, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T03:20:42-08:00","id":842937,"title":"","content":"In addition, Aegis, Veritas, and Ms Stitch all unlocked the first keys to their Ciphers. See below:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Aegis. Embeds: Like I Built It, Fire Drill<br /> <br /> Home Is Where The Heart Is<br /> Cost: None<br /> Dice Pool: Wits + Crafts<br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> <i>Aegis can ward locations against their enemies. All they need to do is touch a nearby surface, and they will be alerted whenever someone passes with hostile intent.</i><br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: A false alarm rings out, audible to everyone within 100 yards. The Demon\u2019s enemies automatically discern that this is alerting them to the Demon\u2019s presence.<br /> Failure: Nothing happens.<br /> Success: A small arcane symbol is burned into the surface the Demon is touching. This symbol strongly resembles a clock, but the numbers are labelled in an unknown language. Despite the apparent inertness of the symbol, its hands do move to a different position each time an individual looks at it. So long as the symbol exists, the Demon will be alerted anytime a being passes within 10 yards of the symbol. This alert rings out like an alarm only they can hear, and they can automatically discern which of their symbols it came from. This additional alertness grants them an initiative bonus equal to their Primum against any enemy who triggers an alarm for the remainder of the scene. These alarms last until the end of the scene, except for those placed in locations the Demon or one of their Covers considers \u201chome\u201d, which last forever.<br /> Exceptional Success: The Demon gains a brief, momentary vision of the individual who has triggered the alarm, and anyone who may be travelling with them.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Veritas. Embeds: Victory At Any Price, Tag and Release<br /> <br /> To the Victor, the Spoils<br /> Cost: N/A<br /> Dice Pool: Wits + Larceny<br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> <i>Veritas gains understanding through victory, the knowledge of what his enemy most desires. If Veritas defeats an opponent in combat, he may trigger this Interlock to leach secrets from his fallen foe.</i><br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: Veritas renders himself open to the world. He automatically fails the next subterfuge roll he makes, and cannot benefit from his demonic nature in respect to lying until he does so.<br /> Failure: Nothing happens. Veritas may not attempt this Interlock again until he wins another combat.<br /> Success: Veritas learns the nature and location of something precious to his defeated enemy. The defeated foe must know the location of the precious thing themselves in order for him to extract this information.<br /> Exceptional Success: Veritas removes knowledge of this thing from the target\u2019s mind. For the next 24 hours, they will not seek to locate or protect it.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Ms Stitch. Embeds: Synthesis, Cause and Effect<br /> <br /> The Scene\u2019s Master<br /> Cost: N/A<br /> Dice Pool: Intelligence + Science<br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> <i>Ms Stitch can manipulate the world around her to an astonishing degree, her mind slipping through arcane channels and twisting events in her favour.</i><br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: Ms Stitch\u2019s efforts go horribly awry. The Storyteller may inflict an Environmental Tilt on the area designed specifically to impede or injure her.<br /> Failure: Nothing happens.<br /> Success: Ms Stitch exerts her will on the scene, altering the environment and area to suit her needs. She chooses a target and specifies a single existing environmental bonus or penalty that the target is likely to experience on a later action. The environmental penalty will then be increased or decreased by an amount equal to her Primum (although it can never exceed +5 or go below -5) on the target when they make an action that would be affected by the environment. Any subsequent use of this Embed before its effect has triggered undoes the original effect in favour of the new one.<br /> Exceptional Success: At the GM\u2019s discretion, an Environmental Tilt may be inflicted on the scene with an impact on the Skill specified. Note that this Environmental Tilt will affect everyone, even Ms Stitch, equally. This is in addition to the effects of a Success.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T22:56:42-08:00","id":844359,"title":"","content":"Excellent! Awesome visuals for Angels and Demons. Looking forward to the rest of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T14:39:41-07:00","id":847309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825315-the-town-that-ran-like-clockwork-demon-actual-play?p=844359#post844359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent! Awesome visuals for Angels and Demons. Looking forward to the rest of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I really can't thank Aegis's player enough. The art they've done for this game has been truly stellar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T14:40:25-07:00","id":847310,"title":"","content":"Session 5<br /> <br /> Rather than spend a full day waiting for the van to make a move, the Ring decided to move on. Smith and Stitch wanted to investigate this Sister Serenity creature the others had discovered, so Aegis made an offer to introduce them. They headed back the way they had come down the Understate. Mr Smith, having spent some time analysing the means by which angels tried to penetrate his Cover, had learned the Deep Cover Embed. His investigation into his Cipher suggested that, as a Manipulation-based Mundane Embed, it could be the next key in his Cipher. He plugged it in. There was a soul-wrenching grind as the gears of his Cipher caught and jammed, wounding him deeply even as his physical body sat in the car unmoved and unblinking. In a moment of understanding, he knew two things. His next Key was actually Unperson. His final Key was Deep Cover.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Ring made the trip without encountering the Angels in the patrol car again. There was no sign of the teenagers' cars Veritas and Aegis had seen, either. Stitch pulled up at the alcove. Axis remained outside as the others entered, manifesting his radio suite form power to listen in on transmissions in the area. He picked up a large amount of background noise, and a clear message in some kind of machine code. His mastery of electronic language allowed him to decipher it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Priority One. Prevent the biological entity designated Fletcher Lynch from departing zone CF. The escape of other entities in pursuit of this mission is deemed acceptable.&quot;<br /> <br /> Inside, the group found Serenity lying along among the pillows and blankets of her chamber. She looked as if she had been crying. Aegis went to her, and she explained that she was frustrated. She did perk up when she saw the others, new worshippers to add to her flock.<br /> <br /> Mr Smith had manifested Aura Sight and was busy scanning Serenity for any sign of what she could be. She registered as an Angel to his senses, but there was a void where a connection to the God-Machine should be. He figured she must be an Exile. Based on his other readings, he determined that one of her aspirations was to control the church and that her greatest fear was the congregation.<br /> <br /> Armed with that knowledge, he began to ingratiate himself to Serenity, praising her beauty and intelligence as he did so. With a combination of his own charms, promises to help her with the church, and subtle put-downs aimed at Aegis and her other followers, it didn't take long for Smith to get her talking. He wanted to understand how Serenity controlled the Understate. She explained that the Father had built her with access codes to help in her mission, but then cast her out into the world without telling her what that mission was. She wanted to catch His attention again. Her plan was to seize the church of Cole's Ford, where so much of the Father's attention was fixated. She asked that her new followers bring her a young man named Owen Michaels, to help fuel her plot.<br /> <br /> Understanding that Serenity wasn't able to give him access codes to the Understate, Smith was ready to leave. He threw one veiled comment too many at Aegis. The Saboteur, already feeling strangely jealous at his comrade capturing so much of the monster's attention, lashed out. There was a short, quick fight that led to Smith quickly yielding, his eye blackened by a few quick blows from Aegis. Serenity appeared startled by the sudden violence. There was a hurried farewell, and the demons left the Exile alone in her chamber once again.<br /> <br /> It was just past dawn when Stitch's van emerged on the streets of Cole's Ford, lifted from the Understate by Serenity's favour. Prolonged exposure to the Understate was proving insightful to more members of the Ring than just Smith. Axis, Aegis, and Stitch were all progressing quickly through their Ciphers.<br /> <br /> The group returned to their homes and reconvened only a short time later at the Church. They took their seats in the pews by rote and listened to the beginnings of Goodenough Jones's speech. This time, however, the speech was interrupted by a groan near the front rows. A man collapsed, clutching his head, and Goodenough immediately broke off his speech. A crowd started to gather, and the town GP pushed his way through. Ms Stitch was able to get to the front of the crowd, and helped to lift the man to his feet. The doctor asked for help getting the man to his car, and Stitch and a few other members of the crowd helped him through. At the back of the crowd, Aegis was pestering those further forward to find out what was going on. By doing so she was able to get a name, Carlisle Foxworth.<br /> <br /> The sermon was cancelled, and the traditional after-church gathering as well. Smith went to activate Homogenous Memory to manipulate those present into thinking Serenity had done something to gain their faith, but he felt something powerful actively preventing him from doing so. He ceased the attempt before the Angel, as he suspected it was, could determine his location. Stitch, Smith, and Aegis decided to see if they could find Owen Michaels, reasoning that staying on Serenity's good books was a good idea. Axis and Veritas split off from the group, refusing to say why. Aegis was able to find out that Owen was assigned to the skeleton crew at the saw mill, so the three of them set off there.<br /> <br /> Axis figured that, as the bluntest and most transparent of their group, Veritas was the best to trust with the knowledge that Fletcher Lynch was in danger. Axis called ahead, name dropping Carlie Sinclair again to get Fletcher to talk to him. Fletcher sounded worried and refused to say whose name he had written today over the phone. When they arrived at the motel, the reason became clear. He let them into his room and showed them the note.<br /> <br /> &quot;Fletcher Lynch. 11:59:59. Don't be then.&quot;<br /> <br /> Axis quizzed Fletcher for as much information as he could. He asked Fletcher if his notes had ever prevented anyone from dying. Fletcher said they had, but it didn't very often. Looking at the instruction, Axis decided he had a solution. A bolthole's stasis effect would be as good a way as any from removing Fletcher from time long enough for the Broken Clock to pass him by. The only problem was that he didn't trust the Ring at the moment.<br /> <br /> Leaving Veritas to comfort Fletcher, Axis stepped outside and made a call to Will. He explained that he needed a Bolthole and asked if Will had one available, banking on the other Demon's reckless nature to offer one up. He was in luck, Will told him to go to the Butcher's store. She would tell her work she was sick and meet him there.<br /> <br /> Axis went back inside. Veritas had not done a good job of keeping Fletcher calm, but Axis was able to get the man to stop panicking and come with him. He briefly explained the plan to Veritas, and said that he would need to go alone to meet his contact. He left Will's name out of it, giving Veritas no real clue as to where he was going. He left with Fletcher.<br /> <br /> The idea of using a Bolthole did make Veritas think. What would happen if he applied the same trick to one of the Broken Clock's previous victims? Jack Berwick was sure to have inside knowledge about the God-Machine's projects in Cole's Ford, and seemed to be a pretty capable guy. He decided to head over there immediately, and called Stitch to ask if he could make use of her Bolthole. Stitch agreed easily, telling him where it was located and how to get in.<br /> <br /> Axis reached the Butcher's Store on Main Street, where he was greeted by a young kid who'd been paid money to direct him round the back. He went through the back entrance and saw Julian Moat, the town butcher, inside. He asked Julian where Will was, and Julian answered that she wasn't able to make it. He then turned and hauled open the door of one refrigerator, revealing a room that seemed to consist solely of a path between an infinite procession of cow carcasses hung on meat hooks. His Ring's bolthole.<br /> <br /> Axis ushered Fletcher inside. When the door was shut behind him, Axis asked Julian some more questions. With a show of reluctance, Julian revealed that he was Will's &quot;other face&quot;, the other part of the Demon called Janus.<br /> <br /> Across town, Veritas was knocking on Jack Berwick's door. When Jack answered, Veritas promptly blurted out the whole story so far, revealing his knowledge of the Broken Clock, the repeating days, Jack's death, and Veritas's own status as a Demon. Jack responded to most of this by levelling a gun at Veritas's chest, but the more Veritas spoke the more information it was clear he had. He talked about the files in Jack's desk about his service for the military and the God-Machine, and details about how the Broken Clock had killed him. For once, Veritas was able to make it through a conversation without his Cover's damaged nature interfering, and he convinced Jack to come with him so smoothly that the former God-Machine agent asked for no further guarantees that what Veritas said was true. They left together, heading for Stitch's abode.<br /> <br /> The rest of the group reached the saw mill, a complex of interlocking red wooden buildings and steel slides. Even from outside the raw of machinery was clearly audible. Stacks of freshly cut lumber sat in the yard on pallets awaiting shipment. A few men could be seen operating forklifts beyond. The entire mill was walled in by a tall concrete barrier topped with razor wire, the only entrance blocked by a traffic barrier manned by a security guard. The guard was known to all the Demons as Egg, a thug and a brute infamous in town for his unpredictable temper. Still, it was no major challenge for Mr Smith. The Authorised Embed got them past on the guise of a surprise Occupational Health and Safety inspection, and they headed straight for the administration offices on the second floor.<br /> <br /> Walking through the saw mill was unnerving. It was possibly the least subtle piece of infrastructure in town, an enormous example of Elimination Infrastructure capable of devouring anything the God-Machine's servants fed it. The scream of machines as they carved entire trees apart was a constant, painful reminder of what the infrastructure would do to them given half a chance. There was more activity than seemed possible given the small handful of workers they could see walking around.<br /> <br /> Once they reached the second floor and stepped through the door to the small, cool set of rooms housing the saw mill's administration, everything went quiet. The rooms must have been soundproof. They could clearly hear the sounds of shouting from the next room, two women almost screaming insults at one another. Aegis triggered Like I Built It to try and work out what was in the next room. Their consciousness filled the saw mill. It had more rooms on the inside than could be physically contained within its walls. Not only that, but they were moving, in almost constant motion, sliding in and out to suit the whims of the mill. Distracted by this, Aegis didn't notice Smith opening the door to the next office and stepping inside until the other Demon had already done so.<br /> <br /> Aegis recognised one of the women involved in the argument. Her name was Leanne Kearson, a thin, neat woman who ran the administration office and was presumably in charge of the mill and its crew over the weekend. The other woman was not known to any of the Demons. She was Leanne's polar opposite, a good decade older at least and obese, heavily tattooed, and wearing loose-fitting and stained black clothes dedicated to some metal band or another. It sounded like they were talking about a computer upgrade that should have been finished by now, but they cut off the moment the Demons walked into the room.<br /> <br /> Leanne had known they were coming, thanks to Egg. When Smith asked to if he could meet with Owen Michaels, she didn't bat an eye. She pulled out a personnel file and opened it, and Smith was able to get a good view of it from his side of the desk. There was a picture of the young man in question, which Smith fixed to his memory. Among his personal details were all kinds of strange asides. &quot;Blood type: Virgin&quot;. An entire paragraph written in a language that was no human script Smith could identify. A time stamp which seemed to be actively counting down as Smith watched it, due to hit zero in about two days' time. After looking at it, Leanne agreed to call Owen up and dismissed the other woman, who she called Rita.<br /> <br /> Owen arrived not long after, a pleasant young man who seemed a bit confused at all the attention. With Leanne's permission they led him to the next room, where Smith activated his Kaleidoscopic Brainwash Interlock and ordered Owen to follow them out of the mill and into their van. They led him away without any fuss.<br /> <br /> They all met up with Veritas and Jack at Stitch's funeral parlour. Smith stayed outside, not wanting to expose himself to Jack. Everyone else was forced to make Compromise checks as Jack immediately realised that they must be the same as Veritas, but no one failed. Instead, Stitch led Jack to the bolthole. Aegis revealed their next Interlock, Quantum Entrapment, could provide some added defences against an Angelic attack. After some discussion about whether doing so would damage the bolthole or not, they secured Stitch's permission to activate the Interlock inside.<br /> <br /> The group was settling down to wait when Axis called Smith, the only one still in cellphone range. Axis had gone in to check on Fletcher and found that he'd written a new letter, addressed to Toni Blum, a corner store owner. &quot;11:59:59, stay off the roads&quot;. Apparently, removing Fletcher from the list of possible targets had caused the Broken Clock to readjust. Axis only gave Smith the information he felt Smith absolutely needed, that Axis's source had given him the name of the Clock's next target. He urged Smith to get the others and try to prevent the next death.<br /> <br /> Veritas wanted Aegis to stay with him and defend Jack, so Stitch and Smith went on their own to Main Street. When Smith explained the message, Ms Stitch's eyes went wide. She explained that one rumour she'd heard that had sounded God-Machine related was that a man in a grey hoodie had been leaping in front of cars on main street. There hadn't been an accident yet though.<br /> <br /> The two of them staked out the area. Just as midday was approaching, they spotted their targets, Toni, an older woman with one prosthetic leg, walking towards the road. At the same time, Smith saw a man in a grey hoodie emerge from between two houses. The two Demons broke into a run to intercept their targets, only to have the wind knocked out of them as they were grabbed by passersby. Smith was grappled from behind by someone who had him on the floor and in a hold before he could blink, unable to twist his head to see who had grabbed him. Stitch was grabbed in a bear hug by Lala, one of Aegis's lumberjack friends, who held him struggling and helpless as the events played out before him. The man in the grey hood stepped into the street. A car swerved. Stitch shouted out to Toni, but she looked for the source of the noise instead of reacting to save herself. The car ploughed into her, and the Demons watched as she was thrown to the pavement and lay still.<br /> <br /> The men holding them immediately let them go. Lala was blinking in confusion, Smith just heard running feet as his assailant fled. Stitch and Lala rushed together to check on Toni, but it was too late to do anything for her. She'd been dead since the moment the car struck her.<br /> <br /> At that exact moment, Veritas and Aegis watched as Jack simply... burst. Blood exploded across them and the walls of the bolthole. There was no angelic presence, no attack, not even a use of magic. Aegis's trap still lay in wait, untriggered. Not even Veritas's Shift Consequences could help, there didn't appear to be any act to shift.<br /> <br /> Axis marked midday without incident. Fletcher remained unharmed. He called the Ring to tell them the good news, that he had found a way to protect people from the Broken Clock, only to hear their stories of failure.<br /> <br /> Upon hearing Smith and Stitch describe their attackers, the Ring decided that the Pie House Infrastructure needed to go. It seemed quite apparent now what the Infrastructure was being used for. Lala had been seen eating there a few cycles earlier, so it appeared to be programming the diners into Sleepers intent on ensuring the Broken Clock's murders went ahead. They had to find the farm supplying the diner, and quickly.<br /> <br /> Everyone piled into Stitch's van, waking up the half-comatose Owen. They drove to the Understate. Aegis tore open the rabbit they had captured a day or two earlier and had been keeping in their own bolthole for just such an occurrence, dedicating its death to Serenity so that she would know to open the Understate. A moment later, and they were once more in the dark.<br /> <br /> They stopped by the Motel Connection to deliver Owen, by this point more than a little freaked out, to Serenity. She practically scooped him up as he entered, promised them a reward, and shooed them from the chamber. From there they continued down the Understate until they reached the car park where the delivery van was parked, still marked by Veritas's Tag and Release.<br /> <br /> There was no sign of any movement, but by this point it was still just mid-afternoon. They had come early to avoid the inevitable blizzard. The Demons set up shifts so that they could rest, with Axis taking the first watch. He sat watching the empty road in silence. His shift passed uneventfully, with the exception when something enormous and insect-like dragged itself across his field of view and on, receding down the tunnel to the west. It had looked as if it were hauling freight.<br /> <br /> Ms Stitch had been unable to sleep. She had the second watch, but so far as she could see nothing of interest occurred. Aegis was next. With the others drifting off, Aegis slipped out of the van to stretch their legs and poke around. Nervous and on edge as they were, they didn't find anything. Later, towards the end of their watch, they did see a procession of ethereal beings, ghosts on a pilgrimage, walking by the side of the Understate. Aegis stayed quiet, and did not catch their attention.<br /> <br /> Mr Smith was on the fourth watch, but the events of the day were weighing heavily on them. He drifted off midway through his own watch, and woke barely in time to wake up Veritas for the final shift. When Veritas woke, however, his eyes went wide. He could sense that the delivery van had gone, that it was somewhere on the surface.<br /> <br /> The original plan had been to follow their quarry out of the Understate. Now they needed Serenity once again. They rushed back to her motel, and Aegis went inside to find Owen naked and passed out face down on the floor. Serenity seemed larger than when they had left, as if she had grown a few feet in height. Veritas provided a direction they needed to exit in, and Serenity granted them their request.<br /> <br /> Back on the road. The Understate faded away. The Demons found themselves on a road of packed earth, a cluster of large buildings in the distance. Veritas could sense the delivery van straight ahead, parked beside a building they were pretty sure was a barn. They weren't quite sure where they were in relation to Cole's Ford, but they'd found it. The farm, the source of the pie meat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T14:50:59-07:00","id":847319,"title":"","content":"So, it turns out that spending a session in close proximity to multiple different sets of Infrastructure and angels/exiles/other things is really, really good for unlocking the Cipher. Smith and Aegis unlocked <i>both</i> their remaining keys.<br /> <br /> Mr Smith:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Interlock # 2 (Remote Link-up, Unperson)<br /> <br /> We Are As One<br /> Cost: None<br /> Dice Pool: Presence + Subterfuge \u2013 target\u2019s Stamina<br /> Action: Reflexive (must make a touch attack first to initiate contact)<br /> <br /> <i>Cover is only one way to travel within the human body, the human soul. Mr Smith\u2019s Demon form could, theoretically, be inside anyone. By becoming potential, he becomes a quantum virus infecting every atom of a target\u2019s being until he arrives at his destination.</i><br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: For a moment Mr Smith is trapped half-in, half-out of physical reality. He must make an immediate compromise check at a -2 penalty and takes lethal damage equal to the target\u2019s Stamina.<br /> Failure: Nothing happens. You must make a Compromise check at a -1 penalty.<br /> Success: Mr Smith must make physical contact with the target mortal. He then disappears. To all extents and purposes, he no longer exists. No power can detect his presence. He has become potential, bound to the target\u2019s body. Upon activating this power, Mr Smith nominates a location or environmental condition. He will only return to physical form when his target enters an area matching the chosen location. He appears and has time for a single instant action before his target can perceive him, although he has no such grace period regarding interactions with any witnesses. If his target is killed or forcefully knocked unconscious (through damage, not by drugs or falling asleep) he reforms early and gains the Shaken Condition. Use of this power is always a Compromise check.<br /> Exceptional Success: There is no need for any Compromise check. In addition, on the turn he reappears, he can make an instant action before coming to the notice of any bystanders.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Interlock # 3 (Unperson, Deep Cover)<br /> <br /> Corrupt the Angelic<br /> Cost: 10 Aether<br /> Dice Pool: Manipulation + Computers + Primum vs Resistance + Rank<br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> <i>To become an angel. To return to the God-Machine\u2019s fold. To do so with one\u2019s Demonic nature hidden inside, ready to return. This is the ultimate expression of Mr Smith\u2019s influence, his pervasive and insidious touch.</i><br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: A screaming siren shatters the air. You immediately gain the Hunted Condition. In addition, the target Angel gains the ability to sense your location until the end of the chapter.<br /> Failure: The attempt fails. The target Angel cannot be targeted by this power again this Chapter. Make an immediate Compromise check.<br /> Success: This Interlock can only activate when Mr Smith is touching an Angel. If successful, he immediately becomes the Angel. He gains access to all of the Angel\u2019s traits. He may not manifest Demonic Form abilities while he is the Angel, nor may he use his Embeds, Exploits, or Interlocks. Mr Smith may return to his normal form at any time as a reflexive action. Doing so causes him to immediately appear beside the Angel. He must immediately make a Compromise Check.<br /> At the end of each scene in which Mr Smith remains inside the Angel he must test to reactivate this Interlock. He does not need to pay the activation cost to retain control.<br /> Exceptional Success: It is possible to Go Loud while Mr Smith is the Angel. Doing so permanently destroys the Angel in the process. If he does not choose to do so, he does not suffer a Compromise Check as the anomalous readings are passed off by the God-Machine as a glitch in the system.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Final Truth:<br /> <br /> What can serve as the Trojan Horse for the most secret library?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Aegis:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Interlock # 2 (Fire Drill, Wavelength Collapse)<br /> <br /> Quantum Entrapment<br /> Cost: 1 Aether<br /> Dice Pool: Dexterity + Survival<br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> <i>Those who intrude on Aegis\u2019s territory must overcome shifting quantum traps built to seize and contain their magic. The more powerful the magic, the stronger the trap becomes.</i><br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The effect rebounds, drawing out the Demon\u2019s Aether at a prodigious rate. The Demon immediately loses Aether equal to its Primum and must make an immediate Compromise check (-1).<br /> Failure: Nothing Happens.<br /> Success: The Demon successfully creates a dangerous trap, set to trigger upon exposure to magic. It can be activated by the use of an Embed, Exploit, Interlock, Demonic Form power, Numen, Influence, Manifestation effect, and any similar use of magical power anywhere in the same location as the trap. Once triggered, the character who used the power may not use any such power for a number of turns equal to their Supernatural Tolerance trait. The Demon may maintain a number of these traps equal to their Primum at any one time.<br /> Exceptional Success: The activation of the trap also inflicts the Stunned Tilt on the target.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Interlock # 3 (Wavelength Collapse, Special Someone)<br /> <br /> Our Future Unleashed<br /> Cost: 1 Aether<br /> Dice Pool: Stamina + Primum (+1 for every Demon Child involved in the scene)<br /> Action: Instant (at least one Demon Child must be present for this power to be activated)<br /> <br /> <i>Demons are merely a step along the path to something new, something greater. You may never live to see the end of this path, but you can catch a glimpse of what the future holds and bring it forth into the present.</i><br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: Something goes horribly wrong. There is a sensation of tearing, as if the future has been irrevocably damaged. Every Demon Child in the scene screams as one, inflicting the Stunned Tilt on everyone present. In addition, the Demon Children are all treated as if they had advanced one condition on the Cipher chain.<br /> Failure: Nothing happens.<br /> Success: This draws on the power within every Demon Child in the area. It supercharges every one of their Embeds in a storm of arcane power, counting as if every Demon Child had simultaneously charged and activated every Embed they possess. The effects in question should be directed in such a manner that, whether the Children are willing or not, the effects of their powers benefit Aegis in some fashion. Afterwards, every Demon Child must check for Compromise.<br /> Exceptional Success: The Demon can decide which Demon Children must check for compromise.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Final Truth:<br /> <br /> Beyond destruction, after devastation, evolution.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Also, Ms Stitch and Axis each unlocked one Key apiece.<br /> <br /> Ms Stitch:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Interlock # 2 (Cause and Effect, Raw Materials)<br /> <br /> Adaptation<br /> Cost: N/A<br /> Dice Pool: Wits + [Skill] (Whichever Skill the item is intended to help)<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> <i>Ms Stitch\u2019s long, cold fingers can twist matter through all kinds of unnatural contortions, the beginnings of a mastery of arcane physics. She can alter mundane pieces of human technology to best achieve its purpose, although doing so leaves the item irrevocably twisted and alien to human eyes.</i><br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The item turns on Ms Stitch, screaming in machine tongues and lashing out at her. She takes two points of lethal damage and the God-Machine\u2019s attention, beginning with the Flagged Condition.<br /> Failure: Nothing Happens.<br /> Success: Ms Stitch alters the item in her hands, perfecting it based on her understanding of the universe. It becomes perfect, granting a new equipment bonus as if it were the finest example of its equipment type (usually represented by a +5 equipment bonus). The item is permanently altered by these changes, becoming a sleek creation that is clearly beyond human ability to construct. Compromise checks suffer a modifier equal to the difference between the original equipment bonus and the new equipment bonus as long as this item is on Ms Stitch\u2019s person. These items only provide benefits to Ms Stitch. They provide no equipment bonus at all, not even their original benefit, to anyone else.<br /> Exceptional Success: Ms Stitch is able to make the item intuitive enough for anyone else to use.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Axis:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Interlock # 1 (Fungible Knowledge, Diversion)<br /> <br /> White Noise<br /> Cost: N/A<br /> Dice Pool: Intelligence + Academics<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> <i>Axis can discharge a wave of static into the minds of everyone around him, creating a buzzing distraction to give him an edge in any situation.</i><br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: An individual making an action that will have a detrimental impact on Axis gains an Exceptional Success if they get even one success on that action.<br /> Failure: Nothing happens.<br /> Success: Activating this Interlock scrambles the thought patterns of everyone in the area. Everyone except Axis must make an immediate Resolve + Composure roll with a penalty equal to successes rolled on this dice. If they fail they suffer the Unskilled penalty on the next action they make.<br /> Exceptional Success: The penalty increases by one.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Phew, that was a lot. If next session goes anything like this last one then I'd expect everyone to have completed their Ciphers by the end of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T03:00:56-07:00","id":850472,"title":"","content":"Session 6<br /> <br /> (Mr Smith's player only joined us at the very end, for for most of this session it was assumed that he was sticking near the van and using Homogenous Memory to remove himself from the scene.)<br /> <br /> The Ring eyed the farm nervously. There were four distinct buildings, and the Deliverer's van was parked beside the largest barn. There wasn't much in the way of cover, the cover of the forest was a good hundred metres behind them and a wide open stretch of ground lay in front. Stitch pulled her van over and shut off the engine. A quick conversation led to them deciding to leave Veritas behind to guard Stitch's vehicle, while the others proceeded on foot.<br /> <br /> They found that the Deliverer's van was unoccupied. Stitch activated the Sabotage Embed to slow any attempt to leave. They then took up positions hidden behind the corner of the barn, waiting for the angel to leave.<br /> <br /> It took about twenty minutes before the door to the barn opened. The smell that seeped out made the Demons want to gag, the scent of stale urine, manure, and something sharp and chemical. The Deliverer stepped out, wheeling a trolley stacked with plastic boxes, and continued on around the corner of the building towards its vehicle. Before the door could close completely, Stitch, Aegis, and Axis sprinted across the intervening distance and slipped inside.<br /> <br /> Everything was dark. The smell was even worse. They could hear the irregular, erratic sound of metal scraping against metal coming from somewhere above their heads. And something big was in the barn with them. They could feel its breath steaming up the inside the barn. They could see its bulk as a darker mass in the shadows. It twitched and moved, and they got a sense of the immense scale of the creature.<br /> <br /> Stitch partially transformed, activating her Blind Sense ability. She was able to sense vibrations in the air, feeling out the area. The creature dominating the interior of the barn was like some kind of elongated, grossly malformed cow. Its body ran the entire length of the barn, swollen to immense height and girth, and hung suspended from the roof by a harness. Its head, tiny to the point of ridiculousness, was facing them with its jaw hanging open as if it were dislocated. Dozens of vestigial legs twitched along its segmented body, giving the impression of it being some kind of mammalian centipede. Metal scaffolding ran around the room, providing a platform whereby the creature's body could be reached. Stitch could sense that the massive beast was plugged in to all manner of machines and IVs, the drips running from the scaffold to its flesh. Meanwhile, the scraping noises they had heard were apparently the larger beast's carers. They were beings made of delicate mechanical armatures enfolded in cloth, giving them the illusion of humanoid shape when they were little more than steel rods. Their limbs ended in blades and spikes, and a few of them appeared to be carving flesh from the larger animal as it lay there. Rivulets of blood ran down its flanks, and dripped onto the floor.<br /> <br /> Stitch noted that the creatures must be able to perceive them, as they were operating confidently in utter darkness. In a low murmur he described the scene. The others tried to decide what to do, when they heard the sound of the Deliverer's vehicle from outside. Despite the Sabotage Embed, its engine had come to life and quickly began to grow fainter. With no Angel to worry about, the Demons decided to engage in combat. In unison, they each cast aside their Covers and assumed their true forms. Wreathed in the light of burning aether, they fell upon the mantises.<br /> <br /> Stitch's body began to replicate, illusions of dozens of herself appearing throughout the barn. She rushed past several mantises which tried to attack her, taking a heavy blow across her back in the process, and leapt onto the deformed cow's flanks. It tried to shake her off, dislodging one of the mantises that followed her instead. Aegis joined her on the top of the beast, and they fired their weapons down on the creatures trying to catch them. On the floor, Axis grappled with two of the mantises who had gone after him instead. He dissolved one in a burst of acid. Before he could tear the other apart, however, it forced its bladed arm down his throat. Something tore inside, and Axis nearly lost consciousness. It took a great effort, but he was able to stay awake long enough to dismember his assailant and watch the others mow down the remaining enemies.<br /> <br /> They quickly examined the interior of the barn. An analysis of the medical equipment made it clear that the drugs being pumped into the bovine monstrosity before them was what gave the meat pies their mystical potency. As they tried to decide what to do, there was a knock on the door.<br /> <br /> Axis and Stitch resumed their covers, uncompromised by the brief revelation of their true nature. Aegis flew up into the rafters, lurking there with their natural weapons trained on the door. Stitch used the Animate Exploit to raise up one of the still-intact mantises, and had it answer the door. A nervous-looking farmer peered in, squinting against the gloom, and spoke to the mantis as if it were an authority.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm not sure if you chaps need to know, but there's something burning in my fields. I think, I think it might be more your forte.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ducking his head, he made to withdraw. Aegis shot him.<br /> <br /> &quot;No mercy to collaborators,&quot; they said to the others.<br /> <br /> Outside, they found Veritas in his true form, lying in a smoking hole in the ground. Aegis was able to land next to him and noted a cylindrical hole bored in his skull. Stitch deduced that he must have attacked the Deliverer as the angel attempted to leave. What the angel had done was unclear. Veritas appeared to be alive and healthy. They decided to take him back to Stitch's van. His demon form was cloaked in its mantle of fire, so only Aegis was able to withstand the heat long enough to dump him nearby. They were about to return and destroy the barn, when Aegis spotted five bright lights descending quickly towards their location. They tried to smother Veritas's flames with the rug in the back of Stitch's van, as Aegis retook their human form and drove them away from the farm. Looking back through the rear mirror, they could see the lights converging on the barn.<br /> <br /> They weren't far from the logging camps, but ultimately the group decided to make the drive back to Cole's Ford. They stuck the still-unconscious Veritas in the furnace at Stitch's place while he burned, located Smith, and briefed him on the situation. Ultimately, only Stitch and Aegis went to Church that morning, Aegis bringing Elise along for the first time since the first day. Midway through the ceremony, the Demons felt some kind of power seeking to strip away their covers. They spoofed the effect successfully, but it was not reassuring. The God-Machine seemed to be taking an ever-closer interest in events.<br /> <br /> Aegis had arranged to meet with their contact, Breeder, at the after-church meeting. Breeder met them wearing the Cover of Bullock, a bare bones Cover of a local postal worker. Aegis introduced Breeder to Elise, and Breeder immediately took a close interest in her. After taking a few Embed-related precautions, the two exchanged information. Aegis revealed what they knew about the Pie House and the connected farm, and Breeder mentioned that his Ring had located the cause of the blizzard. A flying citadel, more heavily guarded than any facility in town, was causing crop circles when it touched down to refuel in the surrounding area. It was invariably in the air by mid-afternoon, just as the storm started sweeping in. Aegis thanked Breeder for the information and asked for help in destroying the Infrastructure at the farm. Breeder offered to send one of his children.<br /> <br /> Veritas recovered consciousness a short time later, and retook his Cover as Sam. He had indeed attempted to fight the Deliverer when it left, degrading his Cover in the process, but it had struck him blind and then inserted something into the back of his skull. He could not remember anything after that point. Stitch had returned when he regained consciousness, and she explained to him what had happened from their perspective.<br /> <br /> Axis had visited Fletcher in his bolthole and returned with the name of the next target. Joseph Jackson, with the note reading &quot;11:59:59, stop cutting wood&quot;. He contacted Aegis about this, and sure enough, they recognised the name. Joseph Jackson was a friend of theirs, working at the logging camp over the weekend. It was a long drive, if they wanted any hope of getting there in time they would need to leave now. Aegis made a brief phone call to Breeder to ask that his child be ready to go with them now. Breeder agreed, saying that his son would meet them by the road. Veritas, still unsure as to what had been done to him, and Axis, badly injured from the fight with the mantises, stayed behind. Smith, Aegis, and Stitch drove up to the logging camps. Aegis chose to bring Elise and their hellhound, Ajax, with them.<br /> <br /> A man flagged them down by the side of the road, just as Breeder had said he would. He looked to be in his thirties, giving the relatively newborn Demons insight into just how old Breeder must be. He was carrying a large pack, and clambered into Aegis's truck. He introduced himself as Scott, and Aegis had a long chat with him on the drive up. He was careful at first, but when he noticed that Elise was the same as him he described his family in a little detail. Breeder was his mother, the Demon apparently collected Soul Pacts with young women so that he could claim them as Covers and get them pregnant, a long term project intended to produce as many Offspring as he could in a controlled environment.<br /> <br /> The group reached the logging camp. There weren't many people around, but Aegis knew their way around. They found Joseph Jackson behind one of the cabins with only minutes to spare. He was cutting firewood with an axe, a massive pile of chopped wood a testament to how long he must have been working. He was a large, bluff man wearing little more than jeans and a flannel shirt against the cold, but his face was burning red and running with sweat. He didn't acknowledge them as they tried to get his attention, just continuing to swing his axe despite clearly being on the verge of collapse.<br /> <br /> Diplomacy failed. Smith rushed forward to snatch the axe. There was a momentary struggle as Joseph tried to keep swinging, but then he sagged in Smith's arms, almost unconscious. There was a pause, and then a being began to pour from Joseph's back. It looked like a cloud of wood chips and it filled the air with the buzzing of a saw blade. It formed into something resembling humanoid shape. The Demons each reacted based on their own assumptions of what the thing was. Stitch recognised it as an Imperative, Aegis had no idea, and Smith thought he was in the presence of an Angel. As Smith turned to flee, Scott raced forward and the Demons present felt a surge of energy that seemed to cause the creature to solidify. Aegis opened fire a second later, and the blast of their hunting rifle seemed to shred the creature in a single shot. It dispersed, wood chips falling to the ground.<br /> <br /> Stitch helped Joseph to the waiting van, as the other lumberjacks in the camp began to converge on the source of the noise. Aegis, holding their rifle, turned to face them. As they did so, they felt a massive source of aetheric energy manifest almost on top of them.<br /> <br /> The Broken Clock had arrived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T03:03:07-07:00","id":850474,"title":"","content":"In the course of this session, Axis unlocked their third key. They locked it into their Cipher, giving them the following:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Interlock # 2 (Diversion, Voice of the Machine)<br /> <br /> Crossed Wires<br /> Cost: 1 Aether<br /> Dice Pool: Manipulation + Computers<br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> <i>Axis has restored a connection between his mind and the God-Machine\u2019s decision-making algorithms. More importantly, he has worked out how to trigger these algorithms to sound a false alarm. He can use this to spread the Machine\u2019s resources thin and access Infrastructure while the guards are gone, or simply to take the heat off himself long enough to put some distance between him and his pursuers.</i><br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: Axis triggers the God-Machine\u2019s alert protocols and immediately gains the Hunted Condition.<br /> Failure: Axis gains the Flagged Condition.<br /> Success: For the next scene, the target suffers the Hunted Condition. If Axis was suffering the Hunted Condition, he is not Hunted until the end of the scene. If he does not have the Hunted Condition, he gains the Flagged Condition when the scene ends, as the God-Machine retraces its alert protocols and identifies suspects who may have been responsible for triggering them.<br /> Exceptional Success: Axis does not suffer the Flagged Condition.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> They also learned that their final key was Password Entropy, but lacked the Experiences to purchase it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T01:06:16-07:00","id":855559,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Session 7<br /> <br /> Everything seemed to slow for Aegis.The lumberjacks and her Ring moved like they were crawling through treacle. They looked around wildly, noticing that they seemed unaffected. There was movement on the edge of their field of vision. They saw glimpses of the fractured corpus of the Broken Clock, the distorted creature of glass and gears seemingly everywhere at once. Then they heard the roar. One of the lumberjacks, a man Aegis recognised as Tom Beattie, stepped out of the crowd. Like Aegis, he was clearly unaffected by the distortion in space-time around them. Aetheric energy seemed to course up and down his arms. He put his head down and charged.<br /> <br /> Aegis braced themselves. The first fist slammed into their stomach, but Aegis slid backwards a few feet with only a few bruises to show for it. They raised their rifle and hired, the shot clipping Tom and spinning him around. He recovered, rushed Aegis again, and for a second time Just Bruised left them only a little winded from the blow. This time, Aegis's shot took off the top of Tom's head.<br /> <br /> Tom Beattie died. Time resumed. Aegis heard a discordant chime, a sound that rang in their head alongside the words, &quot;Alternate sacrifice actioned.&quot;<br /> <br /> The fight had played out impossibly fast for the others. Smith reacted before anyone else, training his gun on Aegis and ordering them to drop their weapon. He ordered one of the witnesses to check to see if Tom had a pulse, while he placed Aegis under arrest. He was able to intimidate the more belligerent witnesses into backing down with his badge and gun, while he escorted Aegis to Stitch's van. He ordered the lumberjacks to radio the town for medial help, and to inform them that he was escorting a prisoner back to town.<br /> <br /> Scott, Elise, and Ms Stitch were able to pile into the van. Stitch checked to make sure that Joseph was ok as they drove back to town. Aegis and Smith were inside Aegis's truck and driving away before the lumberjacks could ask them any more questions. The Demons discussed their situation quietly, Stitch joining in via Remote Link-Up. They had saved Joseph, but it was clear that the Broken Clock had managed to claim a life anyway by making Aegis shoot Tom. Smith told Aegis that he would need to arrest them to avoid suspicion. The reset at midnight would free them, and Ms Stitch could camp in her bolthole and wake everyone up that night for another crack at disrupting the meat supply.<br /> <br /> Back in town, Axis had been swapping skills around with Fungible Knowledge in a series of experiments to find out what, exactly, had happened to Veritas when he fought the Deliverer. He had little luck at first. By the time the others had returned to town, all he had determined was that there was no apparent marking on Veritas's Cover, so the damage was contained to his Demonic Form. There was a brief conference between the Ring as they settled on a plan for the night. Once that was sorted out Elise was returned to her home and Scott left to report to his father. Ms Stitch took the unconscious Joseph to the GP's office to treat him for his severe exhaustion. Smith completed his arrest of Aegis, shared a few brief words to the clearly overwhelmed Sheriff Moore, and then went to Aegis's home to babysit Elise for the rest of the night.<br /> <br /> \u200bA bit more digging at his library led Axis to the conclusion that whatever had been done to Veritas was not overly dissimilar from the Memory Theft Process. That was cause for worry for the entire Ring. There was every chance that the Angel could have learned all of their identities. The only consolation was that it had not had much time to root around in his skull.<br /> <br /> Stitch emerged from her Bolthole just past midnight and began to call each of the other members of the Ring, waking them all once again for an early morning/late night assault on the farm. Axis was disconcerted to discover that the injuries he had sustained in Demon Form had not reset at midnight, leaving him a whole lot weaker than made him comfortable on the precipice of the attack. Aegis woke Elise and gently calmed her down. They needed to bring Ajax for some added muscle that night, and they weren't comfortable leaving Elise on her own, so they bundled her into their truck.<br /> <br /> The Ring had decided that they would strike before the Deliverer arrived to pick up the meat for the day. Now that they knew the way, they had no need of the Understate to get to the farm. They drove out, arriving at the farm only a short time before the Deliverer was due to arrive. The Ring parked their vehicles, Stitch's van and Aegis's truck, near the tree line and proceeded across the open fields on foot. Smith used Remote Link-Up to connect the Ring to one another. Aegis carried their rifle on one shoulder, Smith's hand was always on his pistol.<br /> <br /> They were only a few metres from the car when every Demon felt their aether reserves begin to drain. By the time they were halfway across the field it was clear that most of the Ring would be completely dry. Stitch stopped and carried out a quick examination on herself. She found a leech attached to her leg, having somehow bored through her trousers. Further examination revealed that, though she had felt nothing, the leech was actually half-buried inside her body. Its head had branched out into a dozen tendrils running beneath her skin, worming its way into her flesh and muscle.<br /> <br /> It quickly became apparent that every Demon, and Ajax as well, was in the same position. Worse, now that they knew what to look for, Aegis could see that the snow-covered fields all around them were filled with the cryptids. Worse still, Stitch could see that tearing the leeches out would leave behind a grievous wound, and cutting them free with her knife was not ideal and likely to leave an open wound of its own. Stitch and Axis got to work though, each removing their respective leeches. Stitch modified their knife with their Adaptation Interlock to make the process easier, and was able to remove them from Smith and Aegis as well. Veritas had been drained of aether, and chose to keep their leech attached rather than go through the painful process of removing it. Besides, the Ring was out in the open and this distraction was eating up valuable time. They pressed on towards the barn.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the leeches proved difficult to avoid. Veritas, who made no effort to avoid them, was soon carrying three or four new passengers. Aegis and Ajax dodged the cryptids, but Smith and Ajax each picked up replacements for the ones they had removed. After a brief conversation Smith, Aegis, and Axis decided to go around the back of the barn and start a fire. Stitch and Veritas could keep watch, while Stitch worked on removing the leeches from Veritas.<br /> <br /> The door to the barn swung open. A woman emerged, swearing at the cold. It was the overweight, tattooed woman Stitch, Smith, and Aegis had seen in an argument at the saw mill. Veritas recognised as her as Rita Manning, a woman he had had some passing contact with over the past few months. She spotted Stitch and Veritas behind their meagre cover and walked over to them.<br /> <br /> &quot;So you two are the ones I was sent to guard against. Alright, get on your feet, into the barn.&quot;<br /> <br /> Veritas narrowed his eyes. An Angel, he supposed. He reached out one hand in a conciliatory gesture, touching her wrist, and tried to activate Wavelength Collapse. It didn't respond. Feeling the leech in his leg writhe, he pieced everything together. The leech wasn't just feeding on his aether, it was also blocking access to his Embeds, Exploits, even his Interlocks and Demonic Form were out of reach.<br /> <br /> The shock kept him quiet. Rita was clearly impatient, shivering violently in the cold. She kicked him roughly in the ribs and ordered him and Stitch to their feet. The two Demons were escorted towards the door.<br /> <br /> On the other side of the building, the rest of the Ring were watching through the others' eyes thanks to the Remote Link-Up Embed. They started to spread the gasoline they'd brought, while Aegis watched their backs. It was Aegis who spotted the ripple in the fields. Up until this point the leeches had been passive, only attaching themselves to those who came close. Now they surged towards the Ring. The Demons had only seconds before the cryptids would be upon them. Aegis struck a match, ordered the others out of the way, and lit the fire. Then, Ajax at their head, they sprinted straight towards the swarm.<br /> <br /> Stitch chose that moment to break into a run, dodging around Rita and rushing back toward the vehicles. Veritas, however, was no great runner. He doubted he would be able to evade their captor in his human form. He reached down, grasped the leeches still attached to him with his bare hands, and tore them from his leg. Skin and flesh came away with them, and blood ran freely down his leg. Without pause, he shed his Cover and assumed his full Demonic Form.<br /> <br /> Rita looked up at him, a mixed expression on her face that was equal parts fear and satisfaction. &quot;I always thought you were one of them,&quot; she said. &quot;Ever since you showed up in town.&quot; She removed an object, Veritas recognised it as a tattoo gun, from her pocket. Seeing him look at it, Rita offered to show him her collection. The Demon, nonplussed, agreed. Rita took off her shirt, revealing her skin was covered in tattoos. She pressed the tattoo gun to her wrist.<br /> <br /> &quot;One last piece to add,&quot; she said.<br /> <br /> Veritas turned his back on her. The rest of the Ring were escaping. He could see through Aegis's eyes that Ajax had cleared a path through the leeches, a blast of razor sharp spines shredding those trying to close in on his master. With his aether reserves still empty, draining through a hole in his system that removing the leeches hadn't plugged, there was nothing Veritas could do to catch up. With lightning crackling around him, he stepped into the barn to ensure that the meat supply was destroyed.<br /> <br /> The enormous cow-like creature stared at him as he approached. Veritas was enormous in his Demonic Form, standing on eye level with the creature in its harness. He laid one hand on it, its skin blistering and burning away under his touch. It bellowed in pain. Behind him, Veritas heard a sound like a dial-up modem's dying cough. He glanced over his shoulder to see Rita leave this world, and something new take her place.<br /> <br /> It still looked like Rita. Her clothes flowed into her skin, giving her a shining, rubbery complexion. Her eyes deformed into monitors, running a stream of machine code. Veritas stepped away from the cryptid, knowing that he was in the presence of an angel. Its name, Dios03, flashed into his mind. It stepped towards him and entered him before he could react, subduing his mind beneath its own with ease.<br /> <br /> The rest of the Ring watched from across the field. Smith cut the feed to their minds the instant the angel possessed Veritas. The fire they had lit was large, but not so large that the barn was likely to be consumed. The angel would no doubt move to suppress it now. They needed to rescue their comrade and ensure the destruction of the barn, or else everything would be for nought.<br /> <br /> Aegis and Axis assumed their Demonic Forms. Smith sat astride Aegis, gun in hand. Stitch readied her van to ram the barn. The flying Demons approached the barn using the dark night as cover. It looked from the sky as if the angel had already put out the fire. They landed close to where the fire had damaged the integrity of the wall and took aim inside, where they could clearly see Veritas walking as if on patrol. Once they received the signal that Stitch was in position through their renewed Remote Link-Up, they attacked.<br /> <br /> Smith's gunshots largely bounced off of Veritas's armour. Aegis activated their Quantum Entrapment Interlock, infusing the space around them with an ability that would lock down Dios03's attempts to use magical abilities. And then Ms Stitch crashed through the barn doors in her van and plowed straight into Veritas. He was hurled into the wall, cracking his head, and crumbled to the ground. The cryptid thrashed in its harness, and Dios03 slid from the downed Demon's unconscious body. Aegis's Quantum Trap triggered, locking the Angel away from access to its magical powers for a vital few seconds.<br /> <br /> Smith kicked a hole in the burnt wall and the Demons rushed inside. Aegis activated Quantum Entrapment, silently giving thanks that they were the member of the group who had retained some measure of aether. Dios03 stared at them in frustration as they clambered up the scaffolding and began to douse the cow-like beast with the only formaldehyde. It began to protest that they would be rewarded if they did not destroy the creature, that it could even help them. Aegis replied, telling it that there was no way they could allow the God-Machine to continue brainwashing the people of Cole's Ford. Dios03 said that without the meat the brainwashing would still continue, but the efficiency would drop. They could destroy the Infrastructure responsible without ever touching the farm. The Demons exchanged glances. Then Smith struck the match.<br /> <br /> Veritas had regained consciousness, his body's self-repair system allowing him to recover. <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The possession, he discovered, had left him with a permanent glitch. All of his cover's old scars and nicks had changed, becoming regular in shape and size as if they had been stamped into his flesh by a machine.</span></span></span> The moment he was back on his feet, Dios03 entered his body again and launched a furious attack on the rest of the ring.<br /> <br /> The cryptid's death throes began to tear the building apart. The fire spread. The Ring beat Veritas unconscious again, and Stitch reversed the van back out of the building. Axis ran outside just before the barn's doors swung themselves shut. Dios03 triggered a third quantum trap in its attempts to pursue Smith and Aegis from the barn, Aegis hauling Veritas along after them. And then they were through, and out into the night.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T01:10:53-07:00","id":855562,"title":"","content":"Axis, Veritas, and Ms Stitch all made progress on their Ciphers (although Veritas lacked the Beats to actually buy their next key). Axis unlocked their final Key, gaining the following:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Interlock # 3 (Voice of the Machine, Password Entropy)<br /> <br /> It Shall Be Mine<br /> Cost: 1 Aether<br /> Dice Pool: Wits + Subterfuge<br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> <i>Axis can call on master codes to Infrastructure, allowing him to disconnect it from the God-Machine temporarily.</i><br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure:<br /> Failure:<br /> Success: The God-Machine ignores that piece of Infrastructure for the rest of the scene. Other Infrastructure relying on its Output will operate to the best of their ability, but will gain no benefit from the Infrastructure. Axis, and other Demons for that matter, will not be noticed in close proximity to the Infrastructure (although they will need to test for Compromise under the usual conditions). Afterwards, the God-Machine may investigate the strange disruption to its operation.<br /> Exceptional Success: The God-Machine does not even notice the missing time in its interaction with the Infrastructure.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> And his Final Truth:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Only scale divides you from the Machine.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And Ms Stitch gained the following Interlock from unlocking her final Key:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Interlock # 3 (Raw Materials, On the Mend)<br /> <br /> Second Life<br /> Cost: 1 Aether<br /> Dice Pool: Intelligence + Medicine<br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> <i>Life is just a mechanism. With this power, Ms Stitch can turn beings of flesh and blood into her clockwork puppets. All she needs is a corpse, some gears, and a disregard for the sanctity of the body.</i><br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The body wakes and immediately tries to destroy the one who dared desecrate it.<br /> Failure: Nothing happens.<br /> Success: The corpse becomes a Clockwork Servitor (see page 133 GMC) with a single modification. She can maintain a number of these servitors per dot of Primum.<br /> Exceptional Success: A second modification may be added to the new Servitor.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> And her Final Truth:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Life is a mere mechanism. Like any broken watch, it can be rewound.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T17:49:08-07:00","id":856106,"title":"","content":"Aegis's player has been knocking out a few more NPC portraits in their spare time, beginning with Sister Serenity (multiple tongues not pictured, but still probably a little NSFW depending on your position on breasts):<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://s188.photobucket.com/user/Azahul/media/Mobile%20Uploads/20160330_195158_1.jpg.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i188.photobucket.com/albums/z27/Azahul/Mobile%20Uploads/20160330_195158_1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T21:41:40-07:00","id":856242,"title":"","content":"Ms. Stitch's long lost cousin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T22:42:00-07:00","id":864128,"title":"","content":"Session 8<br /> <br /> Ms Stitch closed the door on the furnace, locking Veritas somewhere safe while he recovered from his ordeal. The rest of the Ring had dispersed once they got back to town, and were busy getting ready for church. Axis refused to leave his home, but the others all exchanged looks as they walked into the building before they went to their respective seats.<br /> <br /> The service began. It was quiet and sedate, the same speech they had heard in every previous instance of this day. As Goodenough Jones spoke, however, each of the demons felt a pressure on their Covers. Aegis and Stitch recognised it as the same effect that had forced them to Spoof the last time they were in church. The Demons reflexively hid behind their covers, but Smith and Aegis were left exposed. Their Covers held, but they knew that someone or something in the area had gained some inkling of their true nature.<br /> <br /> The two demons were accosted as they left the service. Members of the local Glawson family approached them separately and separated the two demons from the crowd and one another, pulling them gently away to quiet corners as everyone else vacated the church to head next door. The Glawsons, led by their mother and father with the adult children waiting in the wings, mentioned to the Demons of threats being made against Goodenough Jones. They asked whether the Demons knew anything about it. Aegis put on a show of being shocked, and their expression quickly became appalled as the Glawsons made it clear that they suspected them. Over on Smith's side, he revealed his identity as a member of the FBI. He asked if they wanted any assistance in protecting the priest. In each case, the Glawsons appeared satisfied.<br /> <br /> Axis spent church paying a visit to Fletcher. The message Fletcher had written read, &quot;Jesse Gorten. 11:59:59. They will bite the hand that feeds them.&quot; Axis relayed this information to the Ring once they were free from church, and they got to work tracking Jesse down. Aegis activated Special Someone and was able to narrow the field enough by making a few assumptions to locate Jesse at the local mechanics shop. They had a brief conversation with the shop owner, Clara Brett, and met briefly with Jesse. He was a scraggly young man working at the shop part-time. He wasn't particularly communicative, and the Ring came away from their conversation with Clara with the impression that he was a bit of a troubled young man. They set a watch on him and withdrew until it would become apparent how the Broken Clock was going to strike.<br /> <br /> Axis spent the morning resuming his investigation of Mr Gant Timbre, the teacher from the local school with some unusually rhythmic tics. He used the Living Shadow Exploit to follow Mr Timbre on his morning routine, and found that the man's activity in the school was little more than checking inventory and making sure the building hadn't been burgled. Feeling a bit disappointed, Axis withdrew.<br /> <br /> Then Jesse made a move, heading home early. They followed him to a rather nice building in need of a new paintjob. A pack of four dogs waited in the front yard, clearly excited to see him return. The Ring checked their clocks. Only minutes to midday.<br /> <br /> Aegis was able to keep the dogs quiet as the rest of the Ring crept across and snuck into Jesse's home. They were the last one inside, listening to Jesse chopping in the next room. Stitch crept around and struck him with Ellipses to keep him occupied on what, upon observation, turned out to be a hunk of meat.<br /> <br /> Then the dogs started barking. Smith checked the window, and saw three men coming through the front gate. He recognised Lala Chan and two others who had been at the Pancake House in previous days. They ignored the dogs and tried to open the door. When Smith set his shoulder against it, they began to batter it down.<br /> <br /> Midday was almost on top of them. Aegis took Smith's spot at the door, holding it shut for a few more moments. As the attackers readied themselves for a charge, they swung the door open. Two of the men stumbled inside. One of them was frozen in place as Smith activated the Look. The second was grappled by Axis. The third rushed in to help his allies. Aegis slammed the door behind them, but not before a dog slipped by.<br /> <br /> The two sides fought quietly in the corridor, muffled thumps and grunts from where Axis and Lala exchanged fist blows, an oasis of calm in the middle where Smith and one of the men stood locked in place. Stitch rushed in to slow down the third man, just as Lala laid Axis low with a lucky blow to the jaw. Aegis was moving to grab him from behind when they spotted the dog. It had been watching the fight but had stayed uninvolved up until that point. There was a moment where it was like the animal could only be seen through a shattered pane of glass, and then it whirled towards Jesse faster than Aegis's eyes could follow. It rushed at its owner from behind. Aegis triggered Just Bruised in the hopes of saving Jesse's life, the presence of the Broken Clock beating down on his senses. The dog struck at the man again and again. Blood splattered the floor. Then the moment passed, and the dog was sitting on the floor looking at its screaming owner with an expression that could only be described as confusion on its face.<br /> <br /> Aegis walked over. Lala and the other men were coming out of their stupor. The Broken Clock's presence was gone. More importantly, its victim was still alive. Bleeding badly, staring at his dog in shock, but alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T21:22:03-07:00","id":875247,"title":"","content":"Session 9<br /> <br /> The brainwashed men seemed to be in a state of shock. At least Lala had the presence of mind to check on the bleeding Jesse, to make sure he was ok, and that the dog was carefully removed from the scene. The Demons slipped away in the confusion, making plans. The God-Machine was sure to be coming for them now. Smith intended to make his way up to the cabin and call in his Soul Pact with Norman, the others were making for Boltholes and other sanctuaries. But the God-Machine struck first.<br /> <br /> Clouds boiled in the sky. The Demons felt their ears pop, pressure building over their head. Snow swirled around their feet, climbing higher and higher with every passing moment. Bright lights blazed to life, and they half-glimpsed immense, moving rings in the sky above their heads.<br /> <br /> As one, the Ring ran for Stitch's van. Aegis ordered them to make for their home, to pick up Elise. Beams of light swirled around them, and Stitch was forced to activate their Scene's Master Interlock to prevent the icy roads from cutting their journey short. They raced through the snow as it built into a proper blizzard.<br /> <br /> It took the use of supernatural powers and almost supernatural driving, but they reached Aegis's home unscathed. They leapt from the van and ran inside, calling to Elise. The young Offspring had been trained well for emergencies like this and was downstairs with her parent in moments, Ajax at her heels. It wasn't fast enough. They stepped outside to find themselves, and the van, ringed with light. Everything faded.<br /> <br /> Veritas, sealed in Stitch's furnace to recover from his wounds, was startled awake by the sound of knocking. He opened the furnace door to see a face he recognised, the Cover of a Demon named Mr Quiet (last mentioned in Session 1, if you're interested). The Demon was wearing the form of a town clerk, dressed in a crumpled white shirt with suit pants and a black tie.<br /> <br /> &quot;They're onto you,&quot; Mr Quiet said. It was all that needed to be said.<br /> <br /> The pair reached Quiet's car, battling their way through the rising storm. Veritas watched through the rear view mirror as Quiet drove away from Stitch's place. He saw five bright lights converging on the building, and then a single much brighter flash. Quiet caught his attention again.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Machine has your Ring. This will probably be our only chance.&quot; Quiet explained that, since this began, he had been in deep cover aboard the Midnight Spiral, the God-Machine's flying citadel responsible for the daily blizzard and the housing for the machinery used to reset the day. He described the layout of the Spiral to Veritas as they drove. Activating the citadel this early in the day, before it had been fully refuelled, meant that it was going to have to touch down after snatching the Ring. The defences would be powered down, it was their best bet to get aboard, free the other Demons, and destroy the entire structure from the inside out.<br /> <br /> Veritas realised they were driving in the direction of Aegis's home. When they arrived, he could see that the Spiral had come to earth halfway on top of the building, smashing most of it to kindling. Only one wall was still standing.<br /> <br /> It was like the eye of the storm. The blizzard simply stopped around this place, allowing them to see their goal. The Midnight Spiral was a massive structure of concentric metal rings. These rings were in motion even on the ground, masking the centre. Mr Quiet hissed at Veritas to move quickly over open ground. As they ran, Veritas looked back. The five lights were following them.<br /> <br /> They reached the edge of the rings. Veritas picked his moment, and stepped between them just in time to avoid being smashed to pulp. His surroundings changed. The open field, the snow, it was all gone. Now he was in a claustrophobic tunnel, too tall and narrow for humans, with Quiet just behind him. The only lighting came from a pale green luminescence coming from the floor, and the live wires that sparked occasionally from their places embedded in walls that looked almost organic.<br /> <br /> Mr Quiet hissed instructions over Veritas's shoulder as they wound their way deeper into the facility. They had been walking for close to ten minutes before they heard the humming sound coming from behind them. They looked back in time to see a glassy black orb, ringed in what appeared to be a small faraday cage, hover into view. There was a moment's pause and it was joined by four others. Sparks of lightning flew, cloud vapour appeared, and bodies began to build themselves around the orbs. Five monstrous visages, gargoyles or harpies, formed with bones of lightning and flesh of hail and rain and wind.<br /> <br /> &quot;Run,&quot; Quiet yelled, and Veritas watched as the other Demon tore his own Cover apart. In its place was a titan with bronze flesh and four arms, each ending in a massive blade. A rattling clank sounded as the titan's chest slid open, a cannon roared, and smoke filled the room. Veritas ran as his fellow Demon rushed the Angels.<br /> <br /> A room Quiet had called &quot;the Harvest Room&quot; lay just ahead. Veritas could see a frame of hooks and needles hanging from the ceiling, a human-sized space in the middle where a target was to be hung for, well, harvesting. Oblong objects that looked for all the world like a stasis pod from a science fiction movie lay against the far wall. As Veritas stepped across the threshold, the entire room bloomed with light.<br /> <br /> There were several figures in the room now, figures that hadn't been there before. They could only be described as shadows, half-real things with flesh that could only be seen because it was where the light wasn't. It was impossible to make out many details beyond their diminutive statue, large heads, and big, pale eyes. Veritas froze.<br /> <br /> &quot;You are not authorised to be here. Please remove yourself,&quot; spoke one, or maybe all, of the shadows.<br /> <br /> Veritas ignored them. His Ring had to be in this room. He walked past the shadows and threw open the first pod. Inside was Aegis, their Cover intact, coated in some kind of slime with a rubber pipe descending down their throat. Veritas yanked out the pipe and Aegis seemed to wake up, falling to their knees and coughing violently. When Veritas turned to walk to the next pod, he found the shadows circling them. They protested his intrusion once again, and Veritas assumed his Demonic Form.<br /> <br /> The fight did not last long. Each blow Veritas struck shattered the corporeal body of a shadow, and they dissipated with a child-like scream. Aegis finished off the last one, assuming Demonic Form as well. The two Demons quickly opened the other pods, discovering the rest of the Ring as well as Elise and Ajax. It was then that Veritas realised that the sound of combat down the corridor had ceased. He wanted to go back for Quiet, but Axis was monitoring communications going on around them. The intruder was down. One Hunter-Killer was designated damaged, but still fit for operations. It seemed highly unlikely that Quiet was alive.<br /> <br /> The Ring fled instead. Axis activated his Interlock to separate the Midnight Spiral itself from the God-Machine's Infrastructure Network. Communications suddenly ceased between the pursuing angels and the Machine. Aegis in turn activated Like I Built It, determining that they needed to get to the centre of the Citadel to bring the whole thing down. Mr Smith asked if it would not be better to simply escape, but Veritas insisted that Quiet's sacrifice not be in vain.<br /> <br /> It was bitterly cold inside the Spiral's tunnels, and it wasn't long before the Demons were feeling the worst of it. As they travelled further, leaving the outer ring, they found that the tunnels became increasingly inimical to life. One by one they abandoned their Covers and assumed their full Demonic Forms. A viscous, milky fluid filled some of the tunnels to knee height, and those who touched it felt the heat leach from their body even more rapidly than before.<br /> <br /> The Ring had been wandering for more than an hour when Aegis told them they would have to cross through a larger chamber. They approached it cautiously, linked together with Mr Smith's Remote Link-Up Embed, watching the corners and covering one another's backs. There was no attack. Instead they stepped out into the panopticon. It was a circular chamber, maybe fifty metres across, the same tall. The walls were covered in hundreds of screens and monitors, each broadcasting a different feed. At the centre of the chamber, suspended in the very middle, was a large sphere of glass filled with a grey cloud. As they watched they could see human faces, fixed in a rictus of pain, floating within. The faces appeared to be watching the screens.<br /> <br /> The Demons stepped closer. Every screen showed a different feed, but they were all focussed on the same subject. Goodenough Jones was in the centre of every one. Some appeared to show him live, broadcasting from different angles. Others showed past recordings of him. Many appeared to show him in the future, or perhaps simply in past instances of the day. Every screen had a string of code running down the right-hand side, which Axis could decipher with his knowledge of the machine tongue. It was medical information, describing the degeneration of Jones's health due to the progression of HIV. His life expectancy was measured in months.<br /> <br /> Axis shared this information with the others, his mind racing as he realised what it meant. The entire Occult Matrix, the deaths, the mission to freeze Cole's Ford in time, was to keep Jones alive. It might be to keep him alive until a medical cure could be found, or simply to keep the priest around until a future matrix required him, but that was obviously the objective. There didn't seem to be any indication that he knew about this, or that he even knew about the God-Machine, but it was clear that he was important.<br /> <br /> The Angel pursuers had appeared to have lost them now that they had to navigate the Midnight Spiral without the God-Machine's help, so the Demons took the time to absorb some of the aether falling from the central orb. Then they moved on, pushing for a final march on the centre. The route took them through one of the inner rings, and for a brief time they had to march along a narrow walkway running along the outside of the structure to the central orb. It was a perilous walk, with high winds, ice, and a sensation like heavy machinery causing the walkway itself to shudder. The hunting cries of angels could be heard on the winds, and bright, strobing lights pierced the clouds all around them. They couldn't see the ground, it seemed the Spiral was in flight once again.<br /> <br /> Then they were inside again, and the central chamber lay before them. A large, ornate archway that looked like it belonged more in a church than the strange tunnels led into a massive empty room too large to be contained in the Spiral. It had to be at least two hundred metres across, with 12 walls and a domed roof and floor. The entrance was halfway up the wall, a small platform protruding out over a long, long fall to the floor below. In the centre of this chamber they could see two spires, one descending from the roof and the other rising from the floor. Suspended between the two points was a small nest of clockwork about the size of a man's head. Even from this distance, something about the device resonated with the demons. A perfect clock, accurate to a second exactly.<br /> <br /> Ms Stitch was the first to step beyond the portal. The moment she did so, she felt gravity give up its hold. Her final action propelled her into the air, floating above the heads of the others. And as if it were some signal, the room's defender made itself known.<br /> <br /> A thick, clear liquid ran up and down the two central spires. Small pieces of machinery floating in a loose cloud around the spires formed together into a clockwork heart. The fluid absorbed this heart, and with every beat it grew larger and larger. The creature grew larger and larger until it was the size of a small house, its malleable form sprouting and reforming limbs as it rushed through empty air towards them. The folds of its translucent flesh peeled back to reveal the piston-driven fangs of a spider-like maw. It bellowed and charged at Ms Stitch.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"https://api.asm.skype.com/v1/objects/0-weu-d2-0701f6c4d662affa311abd0e61fccd0d/views/imgpsh_fullsize\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://api.asm.skype.com/v1/objects/0-weu-d2-0701f6c4d662affa311abd0e61fccd0d/views/imgpsh_fullsize\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Every Demon save for Stitch found themselves frozen with fear at that first roar. The Clockwork Shoggoth collided with the Demon, biting down on her left arm. Crying out with pain, Stitch kicked back off it and into space, firing blasts of light from the weapon concealed in her right arm. They seemed to bother the angel, but they failed to slow it down. As Stitch fled to use the Platform as Cover, it launched a stream of boiling tar from its mouth. The blast struck Veritas, and Stitch switched targets. Their next attack was aimed at the delicate clockwork almost a hundred metres away. The shot hit and it was as if time skipped forward leaving frozen afterimages behind to show what had happened. At the same instant, a second blast of tar came from where their attacker had first manifested, striking Stitch in the chest and almost killing her outright.<br /> <br /> Aegis regained their senses. They activated their Interlocks, tearing an arcane storm from Elise that slammed into the monster. As it staggered back, Aegis found their relationship to time changing. They could be two things at once, every second a moment that allowed them to attack and retreat, fight and defend. They took flight, launching waves of iron spikes into the attacker.<br /> <br /> Veritas and Axis rushed the creature together, trying to seize it before it could finish off Stitch. Axis reached it first thanks to his wings, and landed on its back, hoping to avoid the brunt of the creature's assault. He was still gravely injured from his earlier fights. Smith, following in their footsteps, launched himself from the platform as he prepared his Corrupt the Angelic Interlock for use.<br /> <br /> Aegis struck again before the others could make their moves. They drove down from the sky, launching another wave of spikes into the beast. This strike seemed to be too much. Its body seemed to harden, then crack, and finally shatter. Aegis folded their wings.<br /> <br /> The Ring, exhausted but all alive, approached the clock together. It had been damaged, slightly, by Stitch's attack, but it was still working. As far as they could determine, the damage would manifest as minor fluctuations in time around the town. A man might be stuck at a traffic light for an hour. Another might find their food go cold in seconds. Strange little events, but not entirely catastrophic.<br /> <br /> Aegis watched the door while the others examined the Infrastructure more closely. It was certainly the device triggered by the Broken Clock to reset the day in Cole's Ford. But, with four Inquisitors to examine the device, they were pretty sure they could turn it to a separate purpose. If one of their number were to connect to the device, they could tear Cole's Ford itself away into a splinter of time, this single day ever-repeating, away from the God-Machine's control and influence. They could be free to rule this one day in time. They could even leave Cole's Ford through the Midnight Spiral, save for the one who bonded to the clock. The others could come and go, using Cole's Ford as a refuge from the God-Machine's grasp, but the one who stayed behind would be there forever.<br /> <br /> Ms Stitch volunteered for that task. She opened her soul, her Primum, and fused it to the device. She saw the day in its entirety, every moment of time in frozen perfection. And then it was gone, stored away, kept forever in her heart. Infrastructure whirred to a halt across town, or else spun in endless loops shedding aether without purpose. Angels vanished or quietly fell as the entire town split away into a splinter of time beyond the Machine's ken. The rest of the ring descended to Cole's Ford, ready to begin a brand new day without fear. <br /> <br /> And in her citadel Stitch watched it all, making plans. There were so many experiments she could run, so many variables she could test in this private world. Every day would be a new experiment, each more radical than the one before. Perhaps, one day, she would begin to change things permanently until Cole's Ford became something entirely new.<br /> <br /> This was her idea of Hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T06:22:17-07:00","id":875551,"title":"","content":"Is it finished, then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T09:18:47-07:00","id":875719,"title":"","content":"I severely doubt it. In fact I think Stitch just set herself up for being an instrument that ends the lives of countless demons.. after all, no Hell is actually safe from the God Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T09:56:06-07:00","id":875735,"title":"","content":"I meant the Actual Play. I could see &quot;Adventures in Hell&quot;, or an Epilogue, or just ending it there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T10:05:20-07:00","id":875741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825315-the-town-that-ran-like-clockwork-demon-actual-play?p=875735#post875735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant the Actual Play. I could see &quot;Adventures in Hell&quot;, or an Epilogue, or just ending it there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly think the game was too short for the story to just end right there, there should be more! ( coming from the guy who did a werewolf campaign that was one continuous story over the course of two and a half years and over 70 3 + hour sessions.. I'm probably asking for too much XD)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T13:21:55-07:00","id":875911,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's the end. The campaign was always designed as a fairly short one, although it could easily have gone twice as long before the players managed to reach the Midnight Spiral.<br /> <br /> As an aside, the conclusion the players came to was that after a few decades of the one endlessly repeating day, Stitch would have started experimenting on the townsfolk. Eventually, Cole's Ford would be some kind of futuristic hellscape where chrome warriors wearing blank visors hunt the surviving unchanged humans with stun beams to drag them back to Stitch's flying fortress for experimentation. Veritas and Axis would probably be leading a gritty band of brothers in a John Connor-esque resistance, while Aegis and Smith would have left long ago before things got really bad. Which all sounds like a wonderfully zany time splinter to throw into a future chronicle, I think <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 04-27-2016, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T15:19:45-07:00","id":876044,"title":"","content":"One question: The day in Cole's Ford repeated, but how did this interact with time outside? 5 repeats = 5 days past, or it is still the same day when you leave Cole's Ford?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T15:56:30-07:00","id":876069,"title":"","content":"The answer is a little variable. Had the characters just shut off the loop, no time would have passed. Had the God-Machine's plan worked, a very long time may have passed. Now, with that they did, it's closer to one day inside leading to one day outside, but Stitch can manipulate that a bit and the damage done to the device could theoretically lead to people from the outside landing in just about any instance of Cole's Ford, while those leaving might find more or less time has passed outside than they expected.<br /> <br /> GM fiat, basically <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'll leave it to you to decide whether that means Game Master or God-Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T20:36:09-07:00","id":876226,"title":"","content":"Oh, Veritas (the only player not to complete their Cipher) also unlocked their second key during the course of the final session. I'll post that up tonight if I remember.<br /> <br /> And there's also one last piece of art that should probably go up, for a character that never made an actual appearance in the story. Seems a shame to waste it though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 04-27-2016, 11:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T20:55:07-07:00","id":876238,"title":"","content":"Any thoughts on bringing the survivors of your various AP all into one setting/game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T21:50:00-07:00","id":876266,"title":"","content":"I'm not the most enormous fan of crossover. World of Darkness games tend to be pretty big and meaty, and it can be hard enough to pack the details of a single splat into a game, let alone trying to integrate others. Like, this campaign hardly even touched on the intricacies of relationships between Demons and separate Rings, and had a party consisting almost entirely of Inquisitors. Hardly more than a skin deep dip into Demon, but there was very little room in there for anything else.<br /> <br /> So yeah, probably not. Currently toying with some vague ideas for a Werewolf or Promethean game (once the latter releases in second edition, I think). I'd really like to use some of the Dust Bowl stuff from Dark Eras in the Promethean game, which rather precludes the appearance of these Demons. And my brain is <i>always</i> thinking up ideas for Mummy, it being hands down my favourite. At least in that last case there's a chance for the Old Gods to make a cameo or two.<br /> <br /> For the moment though, I think my group will be taking the IKRPG for a spin. Got some ideas for a Game of Thrones-esque war of the houses campaign to run there, which should keep us occupied for a while <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T22:01:19-07:00","id":876274,"title":"","content":"IKRPG? Iron Kingdoms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T22:11:30-07:00","id":876281,"title":"","content":"Yep. I'm pretty invested in the tabletop game. Plus I figured something a bit more fantastical would be a nice break from all the urban horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T19:27:28-07:00","id":877246,"title":"","content":"First up, Veritas's second Interlock:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Interlock #2 (Tag and Release, Fractal Reality)<br /> <br /> The Future in Shattered Pane<br /> Cost: None<br /> Dice Pool: Intelligence + Occult<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> <i>Beneath the world\u2019s surface grind enormous gears, functions in an immense computing machine determining the fate of every living man. When Veritas turns his gaze inwards, he sees broken moments of possible futures, fates not lived and destinies that may yet be fulfilled.</i><br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: Veritas opens a connection, and he is seen. The God-Machine knows the next move Veritas will make. He gains the Blown Condition.<br /> Failure: Nothing happens.<br /> Success: A cavalcade of images reveal glimpses of possible futures to Veritas involving the subject he is targeting. He learns the next skill the target intends to use.<br /> Exceptional Success: Veritas gains the Informed Condition relating to interactions with the subject.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"tha